{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c48f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":162,"recorded_at":1780531400000319,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-5148-7662-b906-1b211ed955a2"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-5148-7662-b906-1b211ed955a2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-5148-7662-b906-1b211ed955a2","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2941 line(s) above)\n2942|### 7.5 Required operations\n2943|\n2944|All plugins MUST implement every operation and return\n2945|<code>capability_unavailable</code> when the provider lacks the surface.\n2946|\n2947|Every request and success <code>body</code> is a closed object. The following\n2948|embedded types are part of provider protocol 2.0.0:\n2949|\n2950|| Type | Exact members and constraints |\n2951|| --- | --- |\n2952|| <code>LeaseToken</code> | <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53 &gt; 0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n2953|| <code>WorkspacePaths</code> | <code>map(UUIDv7,absolute-path)[1..256]</code>; paths are destination-native, canonical, and contain no NUL |\n2954|| <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>interactive:boolean</code>, <code>columns:uint16[1..1000]</code>, <code>rows:uint16[1..1000]</code> |\n2955|| <code>ProcessObservation</code> | <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>executable_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>started_at:timestamp</code>, <code>candidate_store_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..256]</code>, <code>candidate_native_ids:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>; no PID is carried |\n2956|| <code>SpawnPlan</code> | <code>argv:array&lt;string&gt;[1..128]</code>, <code>cwd:absolute-path</code>, <code>env_names:sorted unique environment-name[0..64]</code>, <code>env_literals:map(environment-name,string)[0..64]</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code>, <code>extensions:object</code>; argv/literal limits and secret rules equal Section 5.1 |\n2957|| <code>SafeBoundaryProof</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]&#124;null</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean&#124;null</code>, <code>open_child_count:uint53</code>, <code>open_database_handle_count:uint53</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>safe:boolean</code>, <code>blockers:sorted unique enum[0..5]</code> |\n2958|| <code>ValidationEvidence</code> | <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>status:passed&#124;skipped</code>, <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code> |\n2959|| <code>NativeDiscoveryProof</code> | <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code>, <code>discovered:boolean</code>, <code>discovery_root:absolute-path&#124;null</code>, <code>backend_resolved:boolean</code> |\n2960|| <code>ProcessClosure</code> | <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>exit_code:int32&#124;null</code>, <code>remaining_process_handles:sorted unique string[0..256]</code>, <code>final_store_generation:string[1..512]&#124;null</code> |\n2961|| <code>DoctorFinding</code> | <code>severity:info&#124;warning&#124;error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>, <code>remediation:string[1..4096]&#124;null</code>, <code>evidence:documented&#124;probed&#124;accepted_test&#124;provider_contract&#124;inferred&#124;acceptance_required&#124;none</code> |\n2962|| <code>ProviderStoreAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>root_role:durable_store&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>access:capture_source&#124;materialize_destination</code> |\n2963|| <code>AuthorityTarget</code> | <code>authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>relative_path:.&#124;path</code> |\n2964|| <code>ProviderCaptureItem</code> | <code>source_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>source_relative_path:path</code>, <code>manifest_path:path</code>, <code>kind:file&#124;directory</code>, <code>state_class:durable_payload&#124;durable_index&#124;derived_cache</code>, <code>required:boolean</code> |\n2965|| <code>ProviderCapturePlan</code> | <code>capture_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_authorities:ProviderStoreAuthority[1..32]</code>, <code>items:ProviderCaptureItem[1..32768]</code>, <code>excluded_targets:AuthorityTarget[0..4096]</code>, <code>store_generation:string[1..512]</code>, <code>snapshot_requires_closed_store:boolean</code> |\n2966|| <code>ObjectSink</code> | <code>root:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>create_mode:exclusive</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2967|| <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_objects</code>, <code>kind:provider_object_source</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:sha256_loose_v1</code>, <code>access:read_only</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>max_bytes:uint53</code>, <code>max_blobs:uint53</code> |\n2968|| <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code> | <code>authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>kind:provider_transaction</code>, <code>root_path:absolute-path</code>, <code>layout:provider_transaction_v1</code>, <code>access:read_write</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids:sorted unique root-id[1..32]</code> |\n2969|| <code>ProviderTransactionEntry</code> | <code>sequence:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>provider_authority_id:root-id</code>, <code>target_relative_path:path</code>, <code>expected_prior_digest:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>prior_kind:absent&#124;file&#124;directory&#124;symlink&#124;hardlink</code>, <code>backup_relative_path:path&#124;null</code>, <code>applied:boolean</code>, <code>restored:boolean</code> |\n2970|| <code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code> | <code>protocol:urn:ax:protocol:provider</code>, <code>protocol_version:2.0.0</code>, <code>document_kind:materialization_transaction</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>plan_id:digest</code>, <code>state:preparing&#124;prepared&#124;committing&#124;committed&#124;rolling_back&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>entries:ProviderTransactionEntry[1..65536]</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code>, <code>created_at:timestamp</code>, <code>updated_at:timestamp</code>, <code>terminal_at:timestamp&#124;null</code> |\n2971|| <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>materialization_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>transaction_authority_id:provider_transaction</code>, <code>plan_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>state:unknown&#124;prepared&#124;committed&#124;rolled_back</code>, <code>rollback_token:base64url-256+&#124;null</code>, <code>native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof&#124;null</code> |\n2972|\n2973|The <code>SafeBoundaryProof.blockers</code> enum is\n2974|<code>background_unproven</code>, <code>child_process_open</code>,\n2975|<code>database_handle_open</code>, <code>provider_busy</code>, or\n2976|<code>store_unstable</code>. A safe proof requires empty blockers,\n2977|<code>input_blocked</code>, <code>foreground_idle</code>,\n2978|<code>background_idle = true</code>, both counts zero, and non-null boundary and\n2979|store generation. <code>ValidationEvidence</code> arrays MUST be sorted by\n2980|<code>code</code> with no duplicate code. Opaque process handles are valid only\n2981|for the operation lifetime and MUST NOT be persisted or replicated.\n2982|\n2983|The <code>root-id</code> grammar is\n2984|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,63}</code>. Capture authorities are sorted by\n2985|<code>authority_id</code>, have <code>access = capture_source</code>, and are\n2986|unique. Capture items are sorted by <code>manifest_path</code>; each authority\n2987|reference MUST resolve, and\n2988|<code>root_path/source_relative_path</code> MUST remain under that exact root\n2989|after symlink/reparse-point resolution. Items MUST neither overlap nor traverse\n2990|through a symlink. Excluded targets are sorted by authority ID then relative\n2991|path and MUST reference the same authority set. <code>derived_cache</code> is\n2992|included only when Section 8 identifies it as required discovery metadata;\n2993|otherwise it must be excluded. Provider roots that contain credentials,\n2994|machine authentication, runtime sockets, locks, or live ax state MUST be\n2995|rejected even when a plugin names them. <code>ObjectSink.root</code> is a fresh owner-only directory\n2996|created by <code>ax</code>. Under <code>sha256_loose_v1</code>, a plugin writes\n2997|each complete blob with create-new semantics at\n2998|the exact Section 3.2 <code>digest_path_v1</code> relative path\n2999|<code>sha256/HH/REST</code> (two-hex shard, 62-hex leaf).\n3000|It MUST NOT create symlinks, hardlinks, devices, sockets, or any file not named\n3001|by its returned descriptors. The host independently hashes every sink file,\n3002|checks size/limits/exclusions, and only then imports it into the ax object\n3003|store. A plugin never receives the live object-store root.\n3004|\n3005|The destination host, not the peer and not the plugin, constructs both\n3006|materialization authorities. A <code>ProviderObjectSourceAuthority.root_path</code>\n3007|MUST equal\n3008|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-object-sources/&lt;materialization-id&gt;/&lt;provider-id&gt;</code>;\n3009|it is a fresh owner-only directory containing exactly the verified manifest\n3010|closure at the same <code>digest_path_v1</code> paths. The host makes every file read-only\n3011|before invoking the plugin. The authority's manifest IDs, byte/blob limits,\n3012|materialization ID, and provider ID MUST equal the selected checkpoint and\n3013|plan. An extra file, writable file, symlink, digest mismatch, or path supplied\n3014|by a remote request is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3015|\n3016|A <code>ProviderTransactionAuthority.root_path</code> MUST equal\n3017|<code>&lt;state&gt;/provider-transactions/&lt;provider-id&gt;/&lt;transaction-id&gt;</code>.\n3018|It is a fresh owner-only directory, is disjoint from the object source and all\n3019|plan roots, and names exactly the materialization/provider/transaction/plan in\n3020|the authority. Its\n3021|<code>same_filesystem_provider_authority_ids</code> MUST equal the sorted set of\n3022|all <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority IDs used by plan operations. The\n3023|host MUST prove that the transaction root and every named provider-store root\n3024|are on the same filesystem/volume before the first plugin mutation. If one is\n3025|not, provider protocol 2.0.0 fails with <code>atomic_commit_unavailable</code>; it MUST\n3026|NOT fall back to an in-place cross-filesystem copy.\n3027|\n3028|The <code>provider_transaction_v1</code> layout contains only these durable\n3029|paths, plus one same-directory temporary file while atomically replacing\n3030|<code>transaction.json</code>:\n3031|\n3032|~~~text\n3033|transaction.json\n3034|staged/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n3035|backups/<provider-authority-id>/<operation-sequence>\n3036|~~~\n3037|\n3038|<code>transaction.json</code> is the UTF-8 JCS encoding of the closed\n3039|<code>ProviderTransactionDocument</code>. Entries are sorted by sequence and\n3040|are exactly the provider-store operations in the plan. For a pre-existing\n3041|target, <code>backup_relative_path</code> is exactly\n3042|<code>backups/&lt;provider-authority-id&gt;/&lt;operation-sequence&gt;</code>; an absent\n3043|target requires <code>prior_kind = absent</code>, a null backup path, and a null\n3044|expected prior digest. Every other prior kind requires that exact non-null\n3045|backup path and a non-null expected prior digest. A prepared document has every\n3046|entry applied, no entry restored, a non-null rollback token, and non-null native\n3047|discovery. A committed document keeps the applied facts, sets the token to\n3048|null, removes every staged/backup payload from disk, and has non-null\n3049|discovery. A rolled-\n3050|back document has every pre-existing entry restored, every transaction-created\n3051|target removed, a null token, and discovery describing the restored\n3052|destination. The plugin MUST fsync a staged replacement and the\n3053|transaction document, atomically rename any predecessor into its backup, then\n3054|atomically rename the staged replacement into the exact target. Each document\n3055|transition is written to a fresh temporary regular file, fsynced, renamed over\n3056|<code>transaction.json</code>, and followed by a parent-directory fsync where\n3057|the platform supports it. Windows uses replace/write-through semantics with\n3058|equivalent user-only DACLs.\n3059|\n3060|<code>terminal_at</code> is null in <code>preparing</code>,\n3061|<code>prepared</code>, <code>committing</code>, and\n3062|<code>rolling_back</code> states and non-null in\n3063|<code>committed|rolled_back</code> states.\n3064|<code>updated_at</code> never precedes <code>created_at</code>, and terminal time\n3065|never precedes either. Timestamps are diagnostics; state, IDs, entry facts, and\n3066|filesystem verification decide recovery.\n3067|\n3068|Every transaction operation receives the same complete\n3069|<code>ProviderTransactionAuthority</code>. A fresh plugin process locates state\n3070|only through that authority, validates the path and\n3071|<code>transaction.json</code> IDs before acting, and MUST NOT use an ambient\n3072|transaction registry or search another root. A crash while\n3073|<code>preparing</code>, <code>committing</code>, or <code>rolling_back</code> is\n3074|reconciled from the entries to one exposed status before\n3075|<code>materialize-status</code> responds; an irreconcilable entry is\n3076|<code>integrity_failure</code> and retains the root for diagnosis. Prepared\n3077|documents store the rollback token under owner-only permissions so a later\n3078|process can reconstruct the current durable status; terminal documents set it\n3079|to null.\n3080|Commit removes all backups only after durable committed state; rollback\n3081|restores all predecessors before durable rolled-back state. The terminal\n3082|<code>transaction.json</code> receipt remains until the corresponding\n3083|Materialization Journal is terminal and for at least\n3084|<code>sync.staging_retention_hours</code> afterward. Object-source bytes and\n3085|backup/staged subtrees MAY then be removed; live or ambiguous roots MUST NOT be\n3086|garbage-collected.\n3087|\n3088|In <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code>, <code>unknown</code> requires null\n3089|plan/token/discovery; <code>prepared</code> requires all three non-null;\n3090|<code>committed</code> and <code>rolled_back</code> require a non-null plan and\n3091|discovery proof and a null rollback token. The discovery proof in a rolled-back\n3092|status describes the destination after rollback. An operation failure does not\n3093|invent a status state: it returns the protocol failure envelope, and the next\n3094|status request reports the last durable state. An unreadable or\n3095|integrity-invalid transaction MUST fail with <code>integrity_failure</code> and\n3096|MUST be quarantined rather than represented as a successful status object.\n3097|Every provider mutation request that carries <code>operation_id</code> uses the\n3098|single Provider protocol 2.0.0 idempotency key\n3099|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>. An\n3100|identical canonical mutation request MUST return a byte-identical result across\n3101|a fresh plugin process; any changed member is\n3102|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> and MUST cause no new mutation. Observational\n3103|operations, including <code>materialize-status</code>, are evolving reads. They\n3104|use the provider envelope's fresh <code>request_id</code> only for correlation,\n3105|MUST NOT be stored as mutation receipts, and MUST return the durable state at\n3106|the read's reconciliation point even when an earlier identical read returned a\n3107|different phase. For <code>capture</code>, replay verifies/reuses only exact\n3108|digest-named files already present in the same Object Sink and re-emits the\n3109|same manifest/descriptors; an extra or changed file fails integrity. Provider\n3110|<code>fork</code> is side-effect-free and recomputes the same plan. The\n3111|materialize mutations use their durable transaction document as the receipt.\n3112|No operation relies on a searched ambient registry. Transaction IDs and\n3113|mutation operation IDs are caller-supplied and stable across retries. For one\n3114|provider materialization transaction, the <code>operation_id</code> is\n3115|transaction-wide across <code>materialize</code> and exactly one terminal\n3116|<code>materialize-commit</code> or <code>materialize-rollback</code>; a\n3117|<code>materialize-status</code> request omits it and locates the transaction only\n3118|through the caller-supplied materialization/transaction IDs and exact authority.\n3119|Reusing the mutation value across distinct operation tags does not alias their\n3120|recorded results. Within one provider ID,\n3121|an operation ID used by the materialize family identifies exactly one materialization transaction:\n3122|its <code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, plan ID, object\n3123|source, transaction authority, provider-store authorities, lease, activation,\n3124|rollback reason, and all remaining body members are immutable retry input for\n3125|their operation tag. Reusing <code>(operation, operation_id)</code> with any\n3126|different canonical body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>; the plugin MUST\n3127|return the first recorded result or failure and MUST NOT allocate, search, or\n3128|mutate another transaction root. A transaction or materialization ID already\n3129|bound to another operation ID is also <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. There\n3130|is no second tuple- or path-based idempotency key in provider protocol 2.0.0.\n3131|\n3132|The operation body registry is exact. A named schema object means the complete\n3133|validated object, not only its digest. Arrays of schema objects are sorted by\n3134|their canonical identity field and contain no duplicate identity:\n3135|\n3136|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3137|| --- | --- | --- |\n3138|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Provider Manifest object (Section 7.3) |\n3139|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, requested_capabilities:sorted unique capability-name[0..7]}</code> | Provider Probe object (Section 7.4) |\n3140|| <code>launch</code> | <code>{session_record:Session Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, launch_plan:Launch Plan, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3141|| <code>identify-session</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7, provider_id:provider-id, observation:ProcessObservation}</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak, matched_evidence:sorted unique native_id&#124;store_path&#124;provider_event&#124;backend_lookup[1..4]}</code> |\n3142|| <code>quiesce</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{proof:SafeBoundaryProof}</code> |\n3143|| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\n3144|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, proof:SafeBoundaryProof, object_sink:ObjectSink, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, capture_id:UUIDv7, manifest:Transfer Manifest, blob_descriptors:sorted unique Blob Descriptor[0..32768], written_blob_ids:sorted unique digest[0..32768], captured_store_generation:string[1..512], exclusions_applied:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code> |\n3145|| <code>materialize</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan:Materialization Plan, object_source:ProviderObjectSourceAuthority, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:prepared, created_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], merged_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], validations:ValidationEvidence[1..256], rollback_token:base64url-256+, native_discovery:NativeDiscoveryProof}</code> |\n3146|| <code>materialize-status</code> | <code>{materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority}</code> | <code>ProviderTransactionStatus</code> |\n3147|| <code>materialize-commit</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, activation:dormant_validated&#124;owner_resumed, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:committed, backup_removed:boolean, committed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n3148|| <code>materialize-rollback</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, transaction:ProviderTransactionAuthority, rollback_token:base64url-256+, reason:lease_lost&#124;validation_failed&#124;resume_failed&#124;operator_abort&#124;crash_recovery}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, materialization_id:UUIDv7, transaction_id:UUIDv7, plan_id:digest, state:rolled_back, restored_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], removed_paths:sorted unique absolute-path[0..65536], native_discovery_absent:boolean}</code> |\n3149|| <code>resume</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>SpawnPlan</code> |\n3150|| <code>fork</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, source_identity:Provider Identity Record, source_checkpoint:Checkpoint Record, new_session_record:Session Record, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo, terminal:TerminalDescriptor}</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7, result_kind:native_fork&#124;supported_import, planned_native_session_id:string[1..512]&#124;null, spawn_plan:SpawnPlan, requires_provider_materialization:boolean, provenance_verified:boolean}</code> |\n3151|| <code>stop</code> | <code>{identity:Provider Identity Record, terminal:TerminalDescriptor, mode:graceful&#124;force, timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000], lease:LeaseToken}</code> | <code>{closure:ProcessClosure}</code> |\n3152|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, architecture:amd64&#124;arm64, provider_executable:absolute-path&#124;null, identity:Provider Identity Record&#124;null}</code> | <code>{provider_id:provider-id, provider_version:string[1..128]&#124;null, findings:DoctorFinding[0..1024]}</code> |\n3153|\n3154|For <code>launch</code>, the profile and launch plan MUST exactly equal their\n3155|Session Record values. Provider <code>fork</code> is a planning call: it MUST\n3156|NOT write a provider store, allocate an active backend conversation, or start a\n3157|process. Its operation ID is the Session Record's\n3158|<code>fork_provenance.operation_id</code>; an identical retry returns the same\n3159|plan and any changed body is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. The new record\n3160|MUST contain Fork Provenance matching the source/checkpoint and operation, and\n3161|a successful result requires <code>provenance_verified = true</code> and MUST\n3162|NOT describe a blank session. <code>native_fork</code> requires\n3163|<code>requires_provider_materialization = false</code> and MAY have a planned\n3164|native ID when the provider allocates it only at process start.\n3165|<code>supported_import</code> requires\n3166|<code>requires_provider_materialization = true</code>; the coordinator then\n3167|calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\n3168|<code>mode=fork</code> and includes the validated provider plan in the\n3169|destination materialization transaction. In both variants, a new Provider\n3170|Identity Record is authoritative only after native discovery following the\n3171|prepared transaction; the planned ID is an expectation, not an identity\n3172|record.\n3173|\n3174|<code>launch</code>, <code>resume</code>, and <code>fork</code> return plans; the\n3175|trusted terminal backend performs process creation. Plugins MUST NOT return\n3176|secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\n3177|advertised portable-store tuple and MUST separate durable includes,\n3178|machine-local excludes, path-key rewrites, quiescence preconditions, and\n3179|validation steps. Its two request and result variants are closed and disjoint:\n3180|a capture request has no destination platform, destination host, destination\n3181|workspace map, or source manifest; a materialize request has no source\n3182|workspace map. Capture therefore works for the first local checkpoint without\n3183|inventing a destination peer or a source-as-destination sentinel.\n3184|\n3185|The capture result's authorities are the complete provider source-root\n3186|authority for that capture. A materialize plan MUST contain at least one\n3187|Section 10.5 <code>provider_store</code> RootAuthority with\n3188|<code>prepared_for_host_id = destination_host_id</code>. Every such authority\n3189|MUST have the same provider/platform as the request, resolve to a\n3190|destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\n3191|disjoint from ax data/state/cache/runtime roots, task-board staging,\n3192|workspaces, and credential/authentication roots unless an exact child path is\n3193|the provider's documented durable store. A path-key rewrite is keyed by logical\n3194|workspace ID and contains destination-derived non-secret cache-key data, never\n3195|a source absolute path. An unavailable surface returns the common failure\n3196|envelope, not a success body with a null required plan.\n3197|\n3198|The following source-only first-checkpoint body and result are the normative\n3199|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-POS</code> fixture. Their absence of every\n3200|destination member is intentional:\n3201|\n3202|~~~json\n3203|{\n3204|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3205|  \"identity\": {\n3206|    \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3207|    \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3208|    \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3209|    \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3210|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3211|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3212|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3213|    \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3214|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3215|    \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3216|    \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3217|    \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3218|    \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3219|    \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3220|    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3221|    \"extensions\": {}\n3222|  },\n3223|  \"source_platform\": \"macos\",\n3224|  \"mode\": \"snapshot\",\n3225|  \"source_workspace_paths\": {\n3226|    \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/payments-api\"\n3227|  },\n3228|  \"lease\": {\n3229|    \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3230|    \"lease_epoch\": 1,\n3231|    \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3232|  }\n3233|}\n3234|~~~\n3235|\n3236|~~~json\n3237|{\n3238|  \"phase\": \"capture\",\n3239|  \"capture_plan\": {\n3240|    \"capture_id\": \"0198f4c8-0790-72aa-8374-3234567890ab\",\n3241|    \"source_authorities\": [\n3242|      {\n3243|        \"authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3244|        \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3245|        \"platform\": \"macos\",\n3246|        \"root_path\": \"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\",\n3247|        \"root_role\": \"durable_store\",\n3248|        \"access\": \"capture_source\"\n3249|      }\n3250|    ],\n3251|    \"items\": [\n3252|      {\n3253|        \"source_authority_id\": \"codex_sessions\",\n3254|        \"source_relative_path\": \"2026/08/19/rollout-11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555.jsonl\",\n3255|        \"manifest_path\": \"session/rollout.jsonl\",\n3256|        \"kind\": \"file\",\n3257|        \"state_class\": \"durable_payload\",\n3258|        \"required\": true\n3259|      }\n3260|    ],\n3261|    \"excluded_targets\": [],\n3262|    \"store_generation\": \"closed:11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555:1\",\n3263|    \"snapshot_requires_closed_store\": true\n3264|  },\n3265|  \"include_classes\": [\"durable_payload\"],\n3266|  \"exclude_classes\": [\"credential\",\"live_pid\",\"machine_auth\",\"socket\",\"transient_lock\"]\n3267|}\n3268|~~~\n3269|\n3270|<code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N1</code> adds\n3271|<code>destination_platform</code> to the capture body and MUST fail with\n3272|<code>incompatible_schema</code>. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N2</code> changes\n3273|the item authority to an undeclared ID and MUST fail before any provider byte\n3274|is read. <code>PROVIDER-PLAN-CAPTURE-N3</code> makes the source authority equal\n3275|the credential root and MUST fail with <code>secret_policy_violation</code>.\n3276|\n3277|<code>capture</code> is the only provider operation that may emit provider\n3278|payload bytes. It requires <code>proof.safe = true</code>, equal proof/plan store\n3279|generation, and the current lease. Its manifest MUST have\n3280|<code>kind = provider</code>, the session as subject, and exactly the returned\n3281|descriptor/blob closure. The host MUST reject an extra sink file, missing\n3282|required item, descriptor mismatch, excluded class/path, generation change, or\n3283|secret-policy violation and MUST discard the isolated sink without importing\n3284|it. The plugin MUST NOT write a live ax store, live SQLite index, credential\n3285|root, or destination native store during capture.\n3286|\n3287|Provider materialization is a recoverable two-decision transaction.\n3288|<code>materialize</code> applies the exact plan while retaining every replaced\n3289|destination byte under the authorized transaction layout and returns\n3290|<code>state = prepared</code>; it MUST NOT delete its backup. While prepared,\n3291|the host validates exact native discovery and either keeps the replica dormant\n3292|or starts the winning owner. It then calls <code>materialize-commit</code> to\n3293|discard the backup, or <code>materialize-rollback</code> to restore it. Commit\n3294|requires <code>backup_removed = true</code>; rollback requires the native\n3295|identity introduced by the transaction to be absent afterward unless it was a\n3296|pre-existing backend identity. A rollback token is machine-local recovery\n3297|authority, MUST be at least 256 random bits, MUST be stored only in the\n3298|owner-only Materialization Journal and prepared Provider Transaction Document,\n3299|and MUST NOT be replicated or logged.\n3300|\n3301|The provider plugin MUST execute only plan operations whose authority has\n3302|<code>kind = provider_store</code> and whose <code>provider_id</code> equals the\n3303|plugin manifest ID. The ax host executes workspace and task-board operations;\n3304|it MUST reject a plugin response that reports any created or merged path\n3305|outside the selected provider-store authorities. The plugin resolves each\n3306|reported absolute path from that authority's root plus the operation's\n3307|relative target, rechecks the predecessor immediately before mutation, and\n3308|uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\n3309|transaction containing disjoint authority-specific executors, not a grant for\n3310|the provider plugin to mutate the workspace.\n3311|\n3312|The three mutation operations use the same parent <code>operation_id</code>,\n3313|<code>materialization_id</code>, <code>transaction_id</code>, and byte-identical\n3314|transaction authority. The sole mutation idempotency key remains\n3315|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code>; the materialization and transaction IDs\n3316|are immutable non-key inputs. Each mutation tag therefore has a distinct key\n3317|while all phases locate the same authority. A retry of one mutation name MUST\n3318|use byte-identical canonical arguments. <code>materialize-status</code> omits\n3319|<code>operation_id</code>; it is the required evolving lost-response recovery\n3320|read and uses the envelope <code>request_id</code> only for correlation. A status\n3321|read MUST reconcile and return the current durable state, so a read that once\n3322|returned <code>prepared</code> may later return <code>committed</code> or\n3323|<code>rolled_back</code>. An unknown transaction MUST return state\n3324|<code>unknown</code>; the host MUST NOT infer success. A prepared transaction\n3325|survives plugin/host restart until explicit commit or rollback. A plugin that\n3326|cannot provide this prepare/status/commit/rollback behavior MUST advertise\n3327|<code>portable_store</code> disabled.\n3328|\n3329|Normative prepared result body:\n3330|\n3331|~~~json\n3332|{\n3333|  \"operation_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3334|  \"materialization_id\": \"0198f4c8-c290-73aa-9374-1234567890ab\",\n3335|  \"transaction_id\": \"0198f4c8-f5c0-76dd-9677-1234567890ab\",\n3336|  \"plan_id\": \"sha256:64644a5ad573d36c0c13f44f56ef25ab93cff33001ff2a3371b082603910f2dd\",\n3337|  \"state\": \"prepared\",\n3338|  \"created_paths\": [\"/srv/provider/sessions/11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"],\n3339|  \"merged_paths\": [],\n3340|  \"validations\": [\n3341|    {\"code\":\"native_discovery\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"detail\":\"exact session identity resolved\"}\n3342|  ],\n3343|  \"rollback_token\": \"YWJjZGVmZ2hpamtsbW5vcHFyc3R1dnd4eXowMTIzNDU2Nzg5QUI\",\n3344|  \"native_discovery\": {\n3345|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3346|    \"discovered\": true,\n3347|    \"discovery_root\": \"/srv/provider/sessions\",\n3348|    \"backend_resolved\": false\n3349|  }\n3350|}\n3351|~~~\n3352|\n3353|The normative transaction cases are:\n3354|\n3355|| Fixture | Calls | Required terminal state |\n3356|| --- | --- | --- |\n3357|| <code>PTX-POS-DORMANT</code> | materialize → status prepared → commit with <code>dormant_validated</code> | committed; replica remains unable to run |\n3358|| <code>PTX-POS-OWNER</code> | materialize → exact discovery → owner resume → commit with <code>owner_resumed</code> | committed; backup removed only after resume evidence |\n3359|| <code>PTX-ROLLBACK</code> | materialize → validation failure → rollback | predecessor bytes restored; introduced identity absent |\n3360|| <code>PTX-LOST-PREPARE</code> | materialize response lost → status prepared | same token/plan returned; no second destination mutation |\n3361|| <code>PTX-LOST-COMMIT</code> | commit response lost → status committed | caller records commit; MUST NOT roll back |\n3362|| <code>PTX-STATUS-EVOLVES</code> | status returns prepared → commit succeeds → the same status body is read under a fresh envelope request ID | second read returns committed; no byte-identical replay rule applies to either observation |\n3363|| <code>PTX-UNKNOWN</code> | status unknown after an ambiguous call | fail closed and quarantine transaction root; MUST NOT infer prepare or commit |\n3364|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-COMMIT</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 status reads the same authority/document → P3 commits and exits → P4 status reads the terminal receipt | prepared and committed facts, token, plan, and discovery are identical across processes; backup bytes are removed only by P3 |\n3365|| <code>PTX-CROSS-PROCESS-ROLLBACK</code> | process P1 prepares and exits → P2 rolls back with the same authority/token → P3 status reads the terminal receipt | every predecessor is restored, every introduced target is absent, and no process searches outside the passed authority |\n3366|\n3367|Changing a plan, object-source authority, or transaction authority on a repeated\n3368|<code>materialize</code>, changing activation/lease on a repeated commit, or\n3369|changing rollback reason/token on a repeated rollback while reusing the same\n3370|<code>(operation, operation_id)</code> key is the normative negative\n3371|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-N1</code> fixture and returns\n3372|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3373|\n3374|<code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N1</code> loses a prepared response and retries the\n3375|same <code>(materialize, operation_id)</code> while changing only\n3376|<code>materialization_id</code>; <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N2</code> changes only\n3377|<code>transaction_id</code>; and <code>PTX-IDEMPOTENCY-ID-N3</code> changes only\n3378|one authority root. Each MUST return <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, leave the\n3379|original transaction document/root byte-identical, and create no second root.\n3380|\n3381|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-LEASE</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-VALIDATION</code>,\n3382|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-RESUME</code>, <code>PTX-ROLLBACK-OPERATOR</code>, and\n3383|<code>PTX-ROLLBACK-CRASH</code> repeat the rollback path with, respectively,\n3384|<code>lease_lost</code>, <code>validation_failed</code>,\n3385|<code>resume_failed</code>, <code>operator_abort</code>, and\n3386|<code>crash_recovery</code>. Each reason is persisted before restoration and\n3387|replaying the same request returns the same terminal result; changing only the\n3388|reason is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n3389|\n3390|Normative <code>resume</code> request body and success body:\n3391|\n3392|~~~json\n3393|{\n3394|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3395|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3396|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3397|  \"operation\": \"resume\",\n3398|  \"deadline\": \"2026-08-19T04:20:00.000Z\",\n3399|  \"body\": {\n3400|    \"identity\": {\n3401|      \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n3402|      \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n3403|      \"record_id\": \"sha256:3667dd9b0ed92b63daa77d848fa5ad77dd8ca3e5a26a47238133e2094fab8f2d\",\n3404|      \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3405|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3406|      \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n3407|      \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n3408|      \"provider_version_range\": \">=0.147.0 <0.148.0\",\n3409|      \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3410|      \"identity_kind\": \"session_uuid\",\n3411|      \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n3412|      \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": null,\n3413|      \"opaque_identity\": {},\n3414|      \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n3415|      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:03:00.000Z\",\n3416|      \"extensions\": {}\n3417|    },\n3418|    \"workspace_paths\": {\n3419|      \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api\"\n3420|    },\n3421|    \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\",\n3422|    \"terminal\": {\n3423|      \"backend\": \"tmux\",\n3424|      \"terminal_id\": \"ax-payments-api\",\n3425|      \"interactive\": true,\n3426|      \"columns\": 120,\n3427|      \"rows\": 40\n3428|    },\n3429|    \"lease\": {\n3430|      \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n3431|      \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n3432|      \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\"\n3433|    }\n3434|  }\n3435|}\n3436|~~~\n3437|\n3438|~~~json\n3439|{\n3440|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\",\n3441|  \"protocol_version\": \"2.0.0\",\n3442|  \"request_id\": \"0198f4c8-e4b0-75cc-9576-1234567890ab\",\n3443|  \"ok\": true,\n3444|  \"body\": {\n3445|    \"argv\": [\n3446|      \"codex\",\n3447|      \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3448|      \"resume\",\n3449|      \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\"\n3450|    ],\n3451|    \"cwd\": \"/srv/relux/payments-api/src\",\n3452|    \"env_names\": [\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"],\n3453|    \"env_literals\": {},\n3454|    \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n3455|    \"profile_mapping\": \"--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\",\n3456|    \"extensions\": {}\n3457|  }\n3458|}\n3459|~~~\n3460|\n3461|### 7.6 Quiescence proof\n3462|\n3463|A successful <code>quiesce</code> response MUST contain:\n3464|\n3465|- provider ID and exact version;\n3466|- <code>input_blocked = true</code>;\n3467|- a provider-specific terminal/idle event reference;\n3468|- <code>foreground_idle = true</code>;\n3469|- <code>background_idle = true</code> when the provider can prove it;\n3470|- open child process and open durable-database handle counts, both zero;\n3471|- the last stable provider-store digest or metadata generation; and\n3472|- <code>safe = true</code>.\n3473|\n3474|If background idleness, process exit, or store closure cannot be proven,\n3475|<code>safe</code> MUST be false and graceful takeover MUST stop. A force\n3476|takeover is a separate operator action; the plugin MUST NOT silently convert the\n3477|request.\n3478|\n3479|For a safe direct-provider proof, Checkpoint Safe Boundary Evidence copies\n3480|provider ID/version, input/idle booleans, and maps\n3481|<code>open_child_count</code> to <code>open_processes</code> and\n3482|<code>open_database_handle_count</code> to\n3483|<code>open_database_handles</code>; <code>evidence</code> is the accepted\n3484|adapter mechanism (<code>provider_api</code>, <code>provider_event</code>,\n3485|<code>managed_pty</code>, or <code>accepted_test</code>). RPC\n3486|<code>SafeBoundary</code> additionally copies the boundary reference and store\n3487|generation, sets <code>store_stable = true</code>, and normalizes\n3488|<code>child_process_open</code> to <code>process_open</code>. No other lossy or\n3489|provider-defined mapping is permitted.\n3490|\n3491|### 7.7 Profile mapping\n3492|\n3493|The v0.3.0 <code>yolo</code> mappings are:\n3494|\n3495|| Provider | Required adapter mapping |\n3496|| --- | --- |\n3497|| Codex | <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> (alias <code>--yolo</code> is accepted by current CLI but the long form SHOULD be persisted in diagnostics) |\n3498|| Claude | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3499|| Gemini CLI | <code>--approval-mode=yolo</code> |\n3500|| Muse | <code>--yolo</code> |\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
