{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":183,"recorded_at":1780531400000361,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3500 line(s) above)\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3502|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3503|\n3504|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3505|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3506|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3507|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3508|probe accepts them.\n3509|\n3510|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3511|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3512|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3513|confirmation controls still apply.\n3514|\n3515|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3516|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3517|\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3558|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3559|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3560|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3561|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3562|\n3563|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3564|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3565|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3566|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3567|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3568|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3569|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3570|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3571|\n3572|The closed operation registry is:\n3573|\n3574|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3575|| --- | --- |\n3576|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3577|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3578|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3579|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3580|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3581|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3582|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3583|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3584|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3585|\n3586|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3587|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3588|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3589|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3590|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3591|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3592|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3593|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3594|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3595|every candidate object.\n3596|\n3597|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3598|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3599|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3600|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3601|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3602|\n3603|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3604|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3605|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3606|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3607|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3608|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3609|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3610|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3611|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3612|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3613|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3614|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3615|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3616|  never paths.\n3617|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3618|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3619|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3620|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3621|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3622|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3623|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3624|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3625|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3626|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3627|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3628|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3629|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3630|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3631|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3632|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3633|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3634|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3635|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3636|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3637|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3638|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3639|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3640|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3641|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3642|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3643|\n3644|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3645|\n3646|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3647|| --- | --- | --- |\n3648|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3649|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3650|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3651|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3652|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3653|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3654|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3655|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3656|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3657|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3658|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3659|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3660|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3661|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3662|\n3663|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3664|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3665|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3666|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3667|and never fallback permission.\n3668|\n3669|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3670|\n3671|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3672|| --- | --- |\n3673|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3674|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3675|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3676|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3677|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3678|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3679|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3680|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3681|\n3682|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3683|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3684|\n3685|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3686|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3687|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3688|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3689|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3690|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3691|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3692|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3693|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3694|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3695|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3696|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3697|never contains executable provenance.\n3698|\n3699|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3700|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3701|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3702|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3703|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3704|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3705|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3706|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3707|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3708|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3709|\n3710|Each capability value contains exactly\n3711|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3712|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3713|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3714|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3715|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3716|\n3717|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3718|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3719|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3720|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3721|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3722|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3723|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3724|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3725|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3726|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3727|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3728|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3729|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3730|\n3731|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3732|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3733|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3734|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3735|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3736|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3737|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3738|write.\n3739|\n3740|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3741|\n3742|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3743|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3744|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3745|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3746|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3747|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3748|\n3749|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3750|\n3751|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3752|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3753|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3754|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3755|\n3756|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3757|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3758|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3759|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3760|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3761|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3762|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3763|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3764|shared.\n3765|\n3766|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3767|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3768|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3769|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3770|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3771|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3772|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3773|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3774|uses an empty body.\n3775|\n3776|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3777|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3778|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3779|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3780|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3781|Error 1.2 has\n3782|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n3783|<code>retryable=false</code>, and then exit with status 6. Only that complete\n3784|response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\n3785|the next lower locally supported major. The response is negotiation evidence,\n3786|not trusted manifest data and not an ordinary retryable operation failure.\n3787|\n3788|Success requires one well-framed success response with every echo exact, a\n3789|complete schema-valid manifest whose <code>supported_protocol_versions</code>\n3790|contains the exact selected version, and process exit 0. A wrong or missing\n3791|echo, malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema, timeout,\n3792|signal, nonmatching exit status, authentication/allowlist failure, integrity\n3793|failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\n3794|MUST NOT cause a lower-major attempt. The caller MUST NOT reinterpret a frame,\n3795|manifest, platform token, request body, or error from one major as another.\n3796|If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\n3797|terminates with its own Structured Error 1.2\n3798|<code>incompatible_protocol</code>, exit 6, and no trusted manifest or partial\n3799|result. These rules select v2 directly, permit v2-to-v1 fallback, support a\n3800|v1-only caller/peer, and terminate deterministically when no major is common.\n3801|\n3802|Transport is one request and one response as line-delimited JSON over\n3803|authenticated local stdio or allowlisted AX SSH. One line is at most 8 MiB.\n3804|The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n3805|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>protocol</code>,\n3806|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3807|<code>operation</code>, <code>deadline_ms:uint53[1..3600000]</code>, and the\n3808|closed operation <code>body</code>. The response echoes protocol/version,\n3809|request/operation. A success response contains exactly the common envelope\n3810|members, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>, with no <code>error</code>\n3811|member. A failure response contains exactly the common envelope members,\n3812|<code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.2.0 in <code>error</code>, with no\n3813|<code>body</code> member. Unknown fields, both or neither branch members, invalid\n3814|UTF-8/JSON, multiple frames, wrong echo, oversize, timeout, or exit without one\n3815|valid response fail with no partial trusted data. Stdout is protocol-only;\n3816|redacted diagnostics use stderr.\n3817|\n3818|The Directory Node Manifest contains exactly schema/version,\n3819|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3820|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3821|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3822|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3823|<code>supported_protocol_versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..16]</code>,\n3824|<code>operations:sorted unique DirectoryNodeOperation[11]</code>,\n3825|<code>schemas:sorted unique ContractAssertion[15..64]</code>,\n3826|<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\n3827|<code>capabilities:map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult)[8]</code>,\n3828|<code>redaction_policy_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n3829|<code>enrichment_profile_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>,\n3830|<code>limits:DirectoryNodeLimits</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. The three\n3831|façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\n3832|contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3833|\n3834|<code>CapabilityResult</code> contains exactly\n3835|<code>status:available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code>,\n3836|<code>reason_code:string[1..128]|null</code>,\n3837|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>,\n3838|<code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Available has a\n3839|null reason; every other status requires one. <code>DirectoryNodeLimits</code>\n3840|contains exactly <code>max_frame_bytes:uint53[1..8388608]</code>,\n3841|<code>max_scan_instances:uint53[1..65536]</code>,\n3842|<code>max_inventory_take:uint53[1..1000]</code>,\n3843|<code>max_excerpt_count:uint53[0..20]</code>,\n3844|<code>max_excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096]</code>,\n3845|<code>max_enrichment_events:uint53[1..5000]</code>,\n3846|<code>max_enrichment_bytes:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n3847|<code>extensions</code>. Both nested objects are closed except for their listed\n3848|reverse-DNS extension maps.\n3849|\n3850|The exact operation registry and bodies are:\n3851|\n3852|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body | Mutation |\n3853|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3854|| <code>manifest</code> | empty object | complete Directory Node Manifest | none |\n3855|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\n3856|| <code>scan</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],prior_batch_id:digest|null,cursor:string[1..4096]|null,max_instances:uint53[1..65536],extensions}</code> | <code>{batch:InventoryBatch,environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,extensions}</code> | directory records only |\n3857|| <code>inventory</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],fields:sorted unique observation-field[1..32],after:string[1..4096]|null,take:uint53[1..1000],extensions}</code> | <code>{observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..1000],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code> | none |\n3858|| <code>preview</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,roles:sorted unique user\\|assistant[1..2],excerpt_count:uint53[0..20],excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096],redaction_policy_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,instance_id:digest,observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,excerpts:PreviewExcerpt[0..20],truncated:boolean,redaction_summary:RedactionSummary,freshness:DirectoryFreshness,extensions}</code> | none |\n3859|| <code>enrichment-plan</code> | <code>{request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{accepted:boolean,expected_input_events:uint53,expected_input_bytes:uint53,expected_model_calls:uint53,disclosure_classes:sorted unique string[0..64],blockers:sorted unique string[0..128],extensions}</code> | none |\n3860|| <code>enrichment-run</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | annotation/job records only |\n3861|| <code>enrichment-status</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,receipt_chain_ids:digest[1..4096],produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | none |\n3862|| <code>continuation-inspect</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,management_binding:ManagementBinding,safe_boundary_status:proven\\|unproven\\|not_required,runtime_status:RuntimeExpectation,warnings:sorted unique string[0..256],extensions}</code> | none |\n3863|| <code>runtime-observe</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{runtime:RuntimeExpectation,extensions}</code> | none |\n3864|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256],include_conformance_age:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],environment_capabilities:map(digest,map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult))[0..256],cloning_contracts:sorted unique ContractAssertion[0..64],extensions}</code> | none |\n3865|\n3866|Each displayed body is closed; its member types, ordering, and limits are the\n3867|registered Section 10.8 schemas and manifest bounds. The <code>probe</code> row\n3868|shown above is the Request 2.0.0 form; Request 1.0.0 differs only in its closed\n3869|legacy platform vocabulary recorded in the major-binding table. The capability\n3870|registry is exactly <code>directory_discovery</code>,\n3871|<code>directory_incremental_scan</code>, <code>directory_head_digest</code>,\n3872|<code>directory_tail_preview</code>, <code>native_title_read</code>,\n3873|<code>native_runtime_observation</code>,\n3874|<code>existing_session_adoption</code>, and <code>native_resume</code>.\n3875|The closed <code>observation-field</code> registry is exactly\n3876|<code>identity</code>, <code>management</code>, <code>head</code>,\n3877|<code>state</code>, <code>workspace</code>, <code>title</code>,\n3878|<code>counts</code>, <code>preview_status</code>, <code>warnings</code>, and\n3879|<code>timestamps</code>. <code>PreviewExcerpt</code> contains exactly\n3880|<code>role:user|assistant</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n3881|<code>text:string[0..4096]</code>, <code>source_event_id:digest</code>,\n3882|<code>truncated:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3883|<code>ManagementBinding</code> contains exactly\n3884|<code>state:managed|unmanaged|conflicted</code>,\n3885|<code>session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n3886|<code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n3887|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n3888|<code>extensions</code>; both IDs and non-empty evidence are required exactly\n3889|for managed, both IDs are null for unmanaged, and conflicted retains all\n3890|evidence without choosing a winner. These nested objects are closed except for\n3891|their listed extension maps. <code>DirectoryNodeBuild</code> contains exactly\n3892|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3893|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3894|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3895|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3896|<code>extensions</code>; every value equals the current manifest.\n3897|Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\n3898|bounds remain safe; head/preview/resume/adoption/write/launch fail closed.\n3899|\n3900|<code>scan</code> and <code>enrichment-run</code> use\n3901|<code>(operation,operation_id)</code> idempotency. Repeating the same canonical\n3902|body returns the prior durable result; a changed body is\n3903|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> without new records. Scan reads only declared\n3904|non-auth roots, publishes observations and its Inventory Batch atomically, and\n3905|never claims that an active prefix is a cloning-safe boundary. Preview requires\n3906|the exact observation/head, defaults to public user/assistant roles, and\n3907|returns bounded redacted terminal-safe text. Raw native IDs and absolute paths\n3908|never leave the source except through an existing AX mutation authority.\n3909|\n3910|## 8. Provider and platform contracts\n3911|\n3912|### 8.1 Matrix notation\n3913|\n3914|Provider and platform matrices use:\n3915|\n3916|- <strong>A</strong>: available from documented or accepted evidence; runtime\n3917|  probe still MUST succeed;\n3918|- <strong>C</strong>: conditional and disabled until the named acceptance gate\n3919|  succeeds for the exact version/platform tuple;\n3920|- <strong>U</strong>: unsupported in v0.3.0 and disabled; and\n3921|- <strong>?</strong>: unknown and disabled because there is no sufficient\n3922|  contract or evidence.\n3923|\n3924|These labels are not aliases. In particular, unknown MUST NOT be rewritten as\n3925|unsupported, and conditional MUST NOT be advertised as available.\n3926|\n3927|### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\n3928|\n3929|| Provider | Durable identity and native location | Resume/import surface | v0.3.0 materialization rule | Required exclusions and limits |\n3930|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3931|| Codex | Session UUID/name; known root <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>. Source absolute cwd is metadata. | <code>codex resume SESSION_ID</code>; current CLI also has <code>codex fork SESSION_ID</code>. | Adapter MUST stage only the closed session objects it has identified, compute the destination cwd mapping, validate discovery by explicit ID, and merge without replacing unrelated sessions. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\n3932|| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\n3933|| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\n3934|| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\n3935|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n3936|| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\n3937|| Qwen through task-board | The task-board bundle and manager-owned provider identity; there is no v0.2.1 direct claim and no v0.3.0 direct <code>ax-provider-qwen</code> claim. | Official task-board open/adopt only. | U for direct native materialization. A task-board prompt-mode bundle follows Section 9 and remains opaque. | All private manager/provider state except bytes included by the official bundle exporter. |\n3938|| Future plugin | Declared by plugin and exact probe. | Declared by plugin. | Every cell starts ?/disabled. Promotion requires Section 19 acceptance evidence. | Common exclusions plus plugin-specific exclusions. |\n3939|\n3940|Muse and Antigravity rows above are normative uses of the accepted\n3941|<code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code> evidence. The controlled Muse placement probe\n3942|does not create a supported import contract. Antigravity backend resolution is\n3943|native resume but not portable storage.\n3944|\n3945|### 8.3 Capability matrix\n3946|\n3947|| Provider | <code>native_resume</code> | <code>portable_store</code> | <code>managed_pty</code> | <code>appserver</code> | <code>task_board_primary</code> | <code>prompt_spawn</code> | <code>native_goal_binding</code> |\n3948|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3949|| Codex | A | C | C | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3950|| Claude | A | C | C | U for direct adapter | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3951|| Gemini CLI | A | C | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3952|| Muse | C by platform/version | U | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3953|| Antigravity CLI | C: backend realm required | U | C | ? | U | ? | U |\n3954|| Pi | A | C | C | U; Pi RPC is not claimed as this capability | ? | ? | U |\n3955|| Qwen through task-board | U direct | U direct | U direct | U direct | U | A through task-board | U |\n3956|| Future plugin | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? |\n3957|\n3958|For Codex and Claude, task-board owns app-server/thread or PTY mechanics,\n3959|reattach, resume, and goal binding. The direct Claude adapter therefore does\n3960|not advertise <code>appserver</code>. The task-board capability plane and\n3961|direct-provider capability plane MUST NOT be conflated.\n3962|\n3963|### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\n3964|\n3965|Each cell is <code>native resume / cross-host materialization / managed\n3966|terminal</code>. Task-board-only behavior is stated separately.\n3967|\n3968|| Provider/platform | Status | Normative limit |\n3969|| --- | --- | --- |\n3970|| Codex / macOS | A / C / C | Resume and unrestricted flag are documented; portable store and PTY flush require adapter fixtures. |\n3971|| Codex / Linux | A / C / C | Same; exact distribution and filesystem fixture required. |\n3972|| Codex / WSL2 | A / C / C | Treat as Linux with a Linux store. Repositories SHOULD live below the WSL home, not a Windows-mounted path. |\n3973|| Codex / native Windows | A / C / C | Native CLI is documented. ConPTY, Windows store discovery, file locking, and sandbox mode MUST pass. Windows 11 is the release baseline; Windows 10 is best effort and requires ConPTY. |\n3974|| Claude / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 2.1.229 help confirms UUID resume and unrestricted flag; store transfer remains gated. |\n3975|| Claude / Linux | A / C / C | Provider family documented; distro/PTTY fixture required. |\n3976|| Claude / WSL2 | A / C / C | WSL is provider-documented; use Linux store and path rules. |\n3977|| Claude / native Windows | C / C / C | Windows 10+ with WSL or Git for Windows is documented, but native PowerShell/ConPTY and native store materialization require acceptance. |\n3978|| Gemini / macOS | A / C / C | Official session root, UUID resume, and session-file surface documented. |\n3979|| Gemini / Linux | A / C / C | Ubuntu 20.04+ documented; other distributions conditional. |\n3980|| Gemini / WSL2 | C / C / C | Linux inference; mounted-filesystem, auth, signal, and path-hash tests required. |\n3981|| Gemini / native Windows | A / C / C | Windows 11 24H2+ documented; PowerShell/ConPTY and path-hash tests required. |\n3982|| Muse / macOS arm64 | A for probed 0.1.0 / U / C | Narrow resume probe accepted; current 0.2.1 and full idle/cron fidelity remain unverified. |\n3983|| Muse / macOS amd64 | C / U / C | Artifact/contract exists; not executed. |\n3984|| Muse / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Official launcher artifacts; not executed. |\n3985|| Muse / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux-path inference only. |\n3986|| Muse / native Windows | ? / U / ? | 0.2.1 artifacts exist, but official launcher and persistence contract do not establish support. |\n3987|| Antigravity / macOS amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Resume works only when the authenticated backend realm resolves the UUID; <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> is documented. |\n3988|| Antigravity / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; keyring/DBus and PTY tests required. |\n3989|| Antigravity / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux inference only; auth, path, signal, and locking tests required. |\n3990|| Antigravity / native Windows amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; ConPTY, data-root expansion, and file-lock tests required. |\n3991|| Pi / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 0.73.1 help verifies session surfaces and default full tool set. |\n3992|| Pi / Linux | C / C / C | Cross-platform Node/package behavior is plausible but exact 0.73.1 acceptance is required. |\n3993|| Pi / WSL2 | C / C / C | Treat as Linux only after path/signal/auth tests. |\n3994|| Pi / native Windows | C / C / C | Provider platform notes exist; exact 0.73.1 store, shell, and ConPTY behavior is unverified. |\n3995|| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\n3996|| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\n3997|\n3998|The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row. An adapter\n3999|accepted in WSL2 does not establish native Windows support.\n4000|\n4001|## 9. Task-board integration\n4002|\n4003|### 9.1 Ownership boundary\n4004|\n4005|Task-board is both a provider-launch abstraction and a distinct persistence\n4006|boundary. <code>tb-sessiond</code> owns private Codex app-server/thread state,\n4007|Claude PTY state, reattach mechanics, provider resume, and goal bindings.\n4008|<code>ax</code> MUST NOT inspect manager databases, private session records,\n4009|provider process files, or authentication state.\n4010|\n4011|The only portable interface is the official\n4012|<code>urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>\n4013|contract. Its initial public creation surface is <code>launch</code>; its bundle\n4014|boundary uses <code>export</code>, <code>import</code>, <code>open</code>, and\n4015|<code>adopt</code>; its public lifecycle controls are <code>status</code>,\n4016|<code>stop</code>, and <code>resume</code>. Until\n4017|task-board advertises this exact bridge version and the required operations,\n4018|task-board takeover MUST report\n4019|<code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>. Existing whole-board archive\n4020|commands are not a substitute.\n4021|\n4022|### 9.2 Official bridge command surface\n4023|\n4024|The required CLI facade is:\n4025|\n4026|~~~shell\n4027|task-board session launch --operation-id OPERATION_ID --request REQUEST_FILE --json\n4028|task-board session status --session SESSION_REF --json\n4029|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode snapshot --json\n4030|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode handoff --json\n4031|task-board session import --operation-id OPERATION_ID --bundle FILE --staging-root DIR --json\n4032|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode dormant-replica --json\n4033|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode fork --new-session SESSION_ID --json\n4034|task-board session adopt --operation-id OPERATION_ID --open-token TOKEN --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --json\n4035|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode graceful --control-token TOKEN --json\n4036|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode force --json\n4037|task-board session resume --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --profile standard|yolo --json\n4038|~~~\n4039|\n4040|Every command MUST print exactly one schema-versioned JSON result to stdout and\n4041|diagnostics to stderr. The bridge MAY use an internal local API, but the\n4042|semantics and bundle bytes MUST be identical.\n4043|\n4044|<code>REQUEST_FILE</code> is an owner-only, machine-local JSON file containing\n4045|exactly the logical <code>launch</code> request body below; the duplicated\n4046|<code>operation_id</code> MUST equal the flag. It contains no credential values\n4047|and MUST be removed after a terminal bridge result. Every mutating facade\n4048|requires the caller-supplied <code>--operation-id</code>; task-board MUST NOT\n4049|replace it with an internally generated value. This makes the exact invocation\n4050|repeatable after a lost response.\n4051|\n4052|The result envelope uses the bridge protocol version independently of the\n4053|bundle schema:\n4054|\n4055|~~~json\n4056|{\n4057|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge\",\n4058|  \"protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4059|  \"operation\": \"export\",\n4060|  \"ok\": true,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae2c-6048-79f1-83fa-e0fa359e30db"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":185,"recorded_at":1780531400000365,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c5bb372d78a2775869aa32e36","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3500 line(s) above)\n3501|| Antigravity | <code>--dangerously-skip-permissions</code> |\n3502|| Pi 0.73.1 | No invented flag; use the provider's default full built-in tool set and report <code>profile_mapping = \"default_unrestricted_tool_set\"</code> |\n3503|\n3504|<code>standard</code> MUST use the provider's normal approval/sandbox behavior\n3505|and MUST omit every unrestricted flag above. It MUST NOT reuse a machine-local\n3506|alias that silently expands to unrestricted mode. Provider-specific standard\n3507|options in a sanitized launch plan are applied only after an exact-version\n3508|probe accepts them.\n3509|\n3510|For Pi 0.73.1, both profiles resolve to the provider's same default full tool\n3511|set because no provider permission-mode flag exists. Probe and launch output\n3512|MUST disclose that equivalence; <code>ax</code> ownership, mesh, conflict, and\n3513|confirmation controls still apply.\n3514|\n3515|The adapter MUST probe the exact provider version before applying a mapping.\n3516|An absent or changed flag fails closed.\n3517|\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n3558|a separately discovered plugin. The Session Adapter owns native\n3559|discovery/capture, canonical normalization, isolated projection, and\n3560|independent read-back. Provider 2 and the AX materializer exclusively own\n3561|live-store mutation, rollback custody, publication, and finalization.\n3562|\n3563|The request envelope contains exactly <code>protocol</code>,\n3564|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, <code>operation</code>,\n3565|<code>deadline</code>, and <code>body</code>. Success contains the first four\n3566|echoed identity fields, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>; failure\n3567|contains them, <code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.1. Body and error\n3568|are disjoint, never nullable sentinels. The protocol inherits Section 7.2's\n3569|JSONL, 8 MiB, deadline, stderr-redaction, and process rules. Invalid envelopes\n3570|are <code>session_adapter_protocol_error</code>.\n3571|\n3572|The closed operation registry is:\n3573|\n3574|| Operation | Permitted authority/effect |\n3575|| --- | --- |\n3576|| <code>manifest</code>, <code>probe</code> | None |\n3577|| <code>discover</code>, <code>inspect</code> | Read-only declared native roots |\n3578|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | Read-only proof; runtime control only for an AX-owned source through Provider <code>quiesce</code> |\n3579|| <code>capture-plan</code> | Fresh isolated plan sink |\n3580|| <code>capture</code>, <code>normalize</code> | Fresh isolated raw/canonical Object Sink |\n3581|| <code>projection-plan</code>, <code>project</code> | Fresh isolated plan/target-object sink; never a live store |\n3582|| <code>read-back</code> | Read-only staged or live authority supplied by core |\n3583|| <code>validate</code>, <code>resume-plan</code> | None; resume-plan returns existing-identity argv/cwd/non-secret environment names |\n3584|| <code>doctor</code> | None |\n3585|\n3586|Every adapter implements every name; an unavailable operation returns\n3587|<code>capability_unavailable</code>, and an unknown name returns\n3588|<code>operation_unknown</code>. Bodies are closed and bounded. Every\n3589|state-bearing call includes a host-created context binding operation, provider,\n3590|Environment Tuple, manifest/executable digests, and request digest. Read\n3591|authorities name host-opened handles, purpose, and expiry, never paths. Object\n3592|authorities name purpose, <code>read|fresh_sink</code>, and hard object/byte\n3593|limits. Partial, malformed, over-limit, or escaped results are errors, never\n3594|absence or fallback permission. Core independently validates, hashes, and seals\n3595|every candidate object.\n3596|\n3597|Every operation body is a closed object. In the definitions below,\n3598|<code>T[n..m]</code> is an array with the inclusive item bound and\n3599|<code>sorted unique</code> means bytewise order of each item's JCS encoding.\n3600|Large data is referenced by manifest or Blob Descriptor ID and MUST NOT be\n3601|embedded in the 8 MiB frame. The reusable closed body types are:\n3602|\n3603|- <code>AdapterCallContext</code> contains exactly\n3604|  <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3605|  <code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>,\n3606|  <code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3607|  <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>, <code>request_digest:digest</code>,\n3608|  and <code>extensions</code>. The host constructs it from the verified\n3609|  candidate. <code>request_digest</code> is the digest of the JCS request body\n3610|  with only that member omitted. Every success echoes the context byte-for-byte.\n3611|- <code>ReadAuthority</code> contains exactly <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3612|  <code>purpose:source_native|target_staged|target_live</code>,\n3613|  <code>root_handle_names:sorted unique string[1..128][1..128]</code>,\n3614|  <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Handle names\n3615|  identify host-opened descriptors or handles delivered out of band; they are\n3616|  never paths.\n3617|- <code>ObjectAuthority</code> contains exactly\n3618|  <code>authority_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3619|  <code>purpose:capture_plan|raw_source|canonical_source|projection_plan|projected_target|read_back_evidence</code>,\n3620|  <code>mode:read|fresh_sink</code>, <code>max_objects:uint53</code>,\n3621|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3622|  <code>fresh_sink</code> requires an empty host-created sink and both limits\n3623|  greater than zero. <code>read</code> exposes only request-named objects.\n3624|- <code>SourceSelector</code> contains exactly\n3625|  <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]|null</code>,\n3626|  <code>logical_workspace_id:UUIDv7|null</code>, and\n3627|  <code>opaque_source_ref:string[1..512]|null</code>; exactly one is non-null.\n3628|- <code>AdapterFinding</code> contains exactly\n3629|  <code>severity:info|warning|error</code>, <code>code:string[1..128]</code>,\n3630|  <code>message:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3631|  <code>remediation:string[1..4096]|null</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3632|- <code>ResourceLimits</code> contains exactly\n3633|  <code>max_objects:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3634|  <code>max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3635|  <code>max_single_object_bytes:uint53&gt;0</code>,\n3636|  <code>max_events:uint53[0..65536]</code>, and\n3637|  <code>max_target_resources:uint53[0..65536]</code>. Each per-item maximum is\n3638|  no greater than <code>max_total_bytes</code>.\n3639|- <code>CapturePlanItem</code> contains exactly\n3640|  <code>native_item_key:string[1..512]</code>,\n3641|  <code>class:capture-class</code>, <code>byte_count:uint53|null</code>,\n3642|  <code>required:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3643|\n3644|The exact request and success <code>body</code> registry is:\n3645|\n3646|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body |\n3647|| --- | --- | --- |\n3648|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 |\n3649|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{expected_provider_id:provider-id,expected_candidate_kind:builtin\\|external,extensions}</code> | Exact Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0; all provider, manifest, version, and tuple equalities below hold |\n3650|| <code>discover</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,workspace_filter:UUIDv7\\|null,limit:uint53[1..65536],cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,sources:CloneSourceSummary[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..1024]\\|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code>; sorted by logical workspace/native Session ID; <code>partial=false</code> iff <code>next_cursor</code> is null |\n3651|| <code>inspect</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source:CloneSourceSummary,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],environment:EnvironmentTuple,ambiguities:AdapterFinding[0..1024],extensions}</code>; zero ambiguities are required before capture |\n3652|| <code>snapshot-proof</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,expected_source_store_generation:string[1..512],allow_provider_quiescence:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,proof:StableSnapshotProof,provider_quiescence_requested:boolean,provider_quiescence_observed:boolean,extensions}</code>; provider quiescence requires both booleans true and separately verified Provider <code>quiesce</code> evidence |\n3653|| <code>capture-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,max_items:uint53[1..65536],max_total_bytes:uint53&gt;0,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_identity:NativeIdentity,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_plan_candidate_id:digest,candidate_count:uint53[0..65536],excluded_classes:sorted unique capture-class[0..9],capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh <code>capture_plan</code> sink containing exactly sorted unique <code>CapturePlanItem[0..65536]</code>, and the two candidate digests are equal after core rehash |\n3654|| <code>capture</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,source_authority:ReadAuthority,sink:ObjectAuthority,source:SourceSelector,capture_boundary:CaptureBoundary,capture_plan_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_plan_digest:digest,source_store_generation:string[1..512],capture_result_candidate_id:digest,source_raw_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,item_count:uint53[0..65536],pre_capture_digest:digest,post_capture_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; fresh raw sink, exact plan-key reconciliation, and an exact included-object closure |\n3655|| <code>normalize</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,raw_objects:ObjectAuthority,canonical_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_candidate_id:digest,canonical_event_candidate_ids:digest[0..65536],raw_reference_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],extensions}</code>; all candidates resolve inside the fresh canonical sink and all raw references are in Capture Manifest closure |\n3656|| <code>projection-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,canonical_event_ids:digest[0..65536],source_objects:ObjectAuthority,plan_sink:ObjectAuthority,target_environment:EnvironmentTuple,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],fidelity_profile:strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only,required_dispositions:closed-map(event-or-artifact-class,sorted-unique-fidelity-disposition[1..7]),forbid_reasons:sorted-unique-string[1..128][0..128],resource_limits:ResourceLimits,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_candidate_id:digest,required_source_object_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],predicted_counts:FidelityCounts,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code>; <code>archive_only</code> is forbidden and every canonical item has one disposition |\n3657|| <code>project</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,source_objects:ObjectAuthority,target_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_candidate_id:digest,created_resource_keys:sorted unique string[1..512][0..65536],actual_counts:FidelityCounts,extensions}</code>; fresh target sink and exact plan/manifest/resource-key reconciliation |\n3658|| <code>read-back</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,projected_object_manifest_id:digest,evidence_sink:ObjectAuthority,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,observed_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple,parsed_event_count:uint53,parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024],workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding,structural_digest:digest,read_back_evidence_manifest_candidate_id:digest,extensions}</code>; staged/live mode is fixed by authority and cannot be relabeled |\n3659|| <code>validate</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,capture_manifest_id:digest,canonical_session_id:digest,projection_plan_id:digest\\|null,projected_object_manifest_id:digest\\|null,read_back_evidence_manifest_id:digest\\|null,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512]\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,mode:staged\\|live\\|archive,valid:boolean,structural_valid:boolean,semantic_marker_valid:boolean,identity_valid:boolean\\|null,workspace_binding_valid:boolean\\|null,resume_surface_valid:boolean\\|null,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],evidence_digest:digest,extensions}</code>; archive requires all four target members null, staged/live require them non-null, and <code>valid=true</code> requires every applicable check true and no error finding |\n3660|| <code>resume-plan</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,authority:ReadAuthority,expected_target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,target_checkpoint_id:digest\\|null,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,target_native_session_id:string[1..512],projection_plan_id:digest,argv:string[1..4096][1..128],cwd_relative:string[1..4096],environment_names:sorted unique string[1..256][0..128],opens_existing_identity:true,extensions}</code>; argv contains no secret, names the trusted CLI family, and contains the explicit identity exactly once |\n3661|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,tuple_registry_digest:digest,refresh_requested:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{context:AdapterCallContext,direction:source_read\\|target_write,registry_sequence:uint53,registry_entry_status:accepted\\|revoked\\|absent,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],healthy:boolean,extensions}</code>; healthy requires an accepted exact binding and every required capability |\n3662|\n3663|Candidate objects are addressed only by their exact\n3664|<code>*_candidate_id</code> in the request's fresh sink. The core retrieves,\n3665|validates, rehashes, and seals them. A partial, malformed, over-limit, escaped,\n3666|or authority-unresolvable result is an error, never an empty or absent result\n3667|and never fallback permission.\n3668|\n3669|Session Adapter Manifest 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly:\n3670|\n3671|| Member | Type and constraint |\n3672|| --- | --- |\n3673|| <code>schema</code> / <code>schema_version</code> | Exact <code>urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-manifest</code> / <code>1.0.0</code> |\n3674|| <code>provider_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}</code>; equal to Provider Manifest and discovered candidate ID |\n3675|| <code>environment_id</code> | <code>[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{0,63}</code>; one semantic native environment |\n3676|| <code>display_name</code> / <code>adapter_version</code> | UTF-8 string[1..128] / SemVer |\n3677|| <code>environment_version_range</code> | Non-empty constraint string[1..256] |\n3678|| <code>platforms</code> | Sorted unique non-empty subset of <code>linux&#124;macos&#124;windows&#124;wsl2</code> |\n3679|| <code>operations</code> / <code>capability_names</code> | Complete ordered registries in this section, no omissions or duplicates |\n3680|| <code>extensions</code> | Reverse-DNS keys; cannot add operations, capabilities, or trust facts |\n3681|\n3682|Its host-computed JCS SHA-256 is\n3683|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest</code> and is not embedded.\n3684|\n3685|Session Adapter Probe 1.0.0 is closed and contains exactly\n3686|<code>schema=urn:ax:schema:session-adapter-probe</code>,\n3687|<code>schema_version=1.0.0</code>, <code>provider_id</code>,\n3688|<code>adapter_manifest_digest</code>, <code>adapter_version</code>,\n3689|<code>environment:EnvironmentTuple</code>, <code>capabilities</code>,\n3690|<code>warnings:sorted unique string[0..2048][0..1024]</code>, and\n3691|<code>extensions</code>. Provider ID, manifest digest, and adapter version equal\n3692|the verified Manifest and host values. Environment Tuple contains exactly\n3693|<code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_version</code>,\n3694|<code>platform=linux|macos|windows|wsl2</code>,\n3695|<code>architecture=amd64|arm64</code>,\n3696|<code>store_schema_fingerprint</code>, and <code>adapter_version</code>; it\n3697|never contains executable provenance.\n3698|\n3699|The exact capability names are <code>native_discovery</code>,\n3700|<code>stable_snapshot</code>, <code>raw_capture</code>,\n3701|<code>canonical_read</code>, <code>canonical_write</code>,\n3702|<code>native_read_back</code>, <code>native_resume_plan</code>,\n3703|<code>official_import</code>, <code>same_environment_lossless_clone</code>,\n3704|<code>tool_history</code>, <code>usage_history</code>,\n3705|<code>compaction_history</code>, <code>subagent_graph</code>,\n3706|<code>opaque_reasoning_roundtrip</code>, and <code>workspace_binding</code>.\n3707|Each value contains exactly status, enabled, evidence, and detail; only\n3708|<code>status=available</code> permits <code>enabled=true</code>.\n3709|\n3710|Each capability value contains exactly\n3711|<code>status:available|conditional|unsupported|unknown</code>,\n3712|<code>enabled:boolean</code>,\n3713|<code>evidence:documented|probed|accepted_test|provider_contract|inferred|acceptance_required|none</code>,\n3714|and <code>detail:string[0..2048]</code>. Missing, extra, duplicated, malformed,\n3715|or contradictory facts invalidate the whole Probe and never mean unsupported.\n3716|\n3717|For source and target, the host seals a closed\n3718|<code>SessionAdapterExecutionBinding</code> containing exactly\n3719|<code>role:source|target</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n3720|<code>candidate_kind:builtin|external</code>,\n3721|<code>canonical_executable_path:string[1..4096]</code>,\n3722|<code>owner_identity:string[1..512]</code>,\n3723|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3724|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3725|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3726|<code>verified_at:timestamp</code>. Before every call and\n3727|target mutation, these facts MUST equal freshly read trusted-candidate facts\n3728|and the Journal binding. A failed/partial read is an integrity failure; no\n3729|self-claim or publisher claim establishes trust.\n3730|\n3731|A target write requires available canonical-write or official-import,\n3732|native-read-back, native-resume-plan, workspace-binding, Provider\n3733|portable-store and native-resume capabilities; exact execution bindings;\n3734|accepted non-revoked signed source/target tuple entries; and current fixture\n3735|plus bounded native-resume smoke evidence. <code>--force</code>, experimental\n3736|profiles, and environment-name-only matches cannot bypass these gates. Unknown\n3737|sources may be archived only after safe byte enumeration; unknown targets never\n3738|write.\n3739|\n3740|### 7.9 Companion Directory Node protocol\n3741|\n3742|Directory Node protocol <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-directory-node</code>\n3743|<code>2.0.0</code> is the current separately negotiated, read-mostly façade\n3744|backed by the same per-environment implementation as Provider 2 and Session\n3745|Adapter 1. Directory Node protocol <code>1.0.0</code> remains an immutable\n3746|legacy wire contract. Neither major adds operations to Provider 2, executes\n3747|Continuation Plans, or transports transcript/workspace bytes.\n3748|\n3749|The exact major bindings are closed:\n3750|\n3751|| Protocol | Request | Response | Manifest | <code>probe.platform</code> vocabulary |\n3752|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3753|| <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>darwin\\|linux\\|windows</code> |\n3754|| <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Request <code>2.0.0</code> | Directory Node Response <code>1.0.0</code> | Directory Node Manifest <code>1.0.0</code> | <code>macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows</code> |\n3755|\n3756|A v1 <code>darwin</code> request denotes the macOS host class defined by that\n3757|published major, but <code>darwin</code> is not a valid v2 wire value and never\n3758|appears in an Environment Observation. A v1 request cannot express WSL2.\n3759|Implementations MUST validate the vocabulary belonging to the negotiated\n3760|major; they MUST NOT relabel a v1 envelope as v2, relabel a v2 envelope as v1,\n3761|or coerce an unknown token across majors. Implementations supporting v2 SHOULD\n3762|serve v1 concurrently for at least one stable specification release. Peers\n3763|choose the highest mutually supported major and fail closed when no major is\n3764|shared.\n3765|\n3766|A fresh adapter invocation has no trusted manifest from which to discover the\n3767|peer's supported majors. The caller MUST therefore enumerate its locally\n3768|supported Directory Node majors in strictly descending numeric order and make\n3769|one <code>manifest</code> request for the highest not yet attempted major. Each\n3770|attempt MUST launch a fresh process; a process that returned or failed an\n3771|attempt is terminated and reaped and MUST NOT be reused for a lower major. The\n3772|request binds <code>protocol_version</code> and request\n3773|<code>schema_version</code> to the exact attempted <code>N.0.0</code> version and\n3774|uses an empty body.\n3775|\n3776|There is exactly one downgrade trigger. The attempted process MUST return one\n3777|well-framed Directory Node failure response whose <code>protocol</code>,\n3778|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id</code>, and\n3779|<code>operation=manifest</code> exactly echo the request and whose response\n3780|<code>schema_version</code> is the bound <code>1.0.0</code>, whose Structured\n3781|Error 1.2 has\n3782|<code>code=incompatible_protocol</code>, <code>exit_code=6</code>, and\n3783|<code>retryable=false</code>, and then exit with status 6. Only that complete\n3784|response-plus-exit tuple authorizes the caller to launch a fresh process for\n3785|the next lower locally supported major. The response is negotiation evidence,\n3786|not trusted manifest data and not an ordinary retryable operation failure.\n3787|\n3788|Success requires one well-framed success response with every echo exact, a\n3789|complete schema-valid manifest whose <code>supported_protocol_versions</code>\n3790|contains the exact selected version, and process exit 0. A wrong or missing\n3791|echo, malformed/partial/extra frame, invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema, timeout,\n3792|signal, nonmatching exit status, authentication/allowlist failure, integrity\n3793|failure, or any error other than the exact downgrade tuple is terminal and\n3794|MUST NOT cause a lower-major attempt. The caller MUST NOT reinterpret a frame,\n3795|manifest, platform token, request body, or error from one major as another.\n3796|If every locally supported major returns the exact downgrade tuple, the caller\n3797|terminates with its own Structured Error 1.2\n3798|<code>incompatible_protocol</code>, exit 6, and no trusted manifest or partial\n3799|result. These rules select v2 directly, permit v2-to-v1 fallback, support a\n3800|v1-only caller/peer, and terminate deterministically when no major is common.\n3801|\n3802|Transport is one request and one response as line-delimited JSON over\n3803|authenticated local stdio or allowlisted AX SSH. One line is at most 8 MiB.\n3804|The request envelope contains exactly <code>schema</code>,\n3805|<code>schema_version</code>, <code>protocol</code>,\n3806|<code>protocol_version</code>, <code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n3807|<code>operation</code>, <code>deadline_ms:uint53[1..3600000]</code>, and the\n3808|closed operation <code>body</code>. The response echoes protocol/version,\n3809|request/operation. A success response contains exactly the common envelope\n3810|members, <code>ok=true</code>, and <code>body</code>, with no <code>error</code>\n3811|member. A failure response contains exactly the common envelope members,\n3812|<code>ok=false</code>, and Structured Error 1.2.0 in <code>error</code>, with no\n3813|<code>body</code> member. Unknown fields, both or neither branch members, invalid\n3814|UTF-8/JSON, multiple frames, wrong echo, oversize, timeout, or exit without one\n3815|valid response fail with no partial trusted data. Stdout is protocol-only;\n3816|redacted diagnostics use stderr.\n3817|\n3818|The Directory Node Manifest contains exactly schema/version,\n3819|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3820|<code>host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3821|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3822|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3823|<code>supported_protocol_versions:sorted unique SemVer[1..16]</code>,\n3824|<code>operations:sorted unique DirectoryNodeOperation[11]</code>,\n3825|<code>schemas:sorted unique ContractAssertion[15..64]</code>,\n3826|<code>environment_tuple_registry_id:digest</code>,\n3827|<code>capabilities:map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult)[8]</code>,\n3828|<code>redaction_policy_ids:sorted unique digest[1..64]</code>,\n3829|<code>enrichment_profile_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>,\n3830|<code>limits:DirectoryNodeLimits</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. The three\n3831|façade executable/module bindings and tuple declarations MUST agree; a\n3832|contradiction is <code>integrity_failure</code>.\n3833|\n3834|<code>CapabilityResult</code> contains exactly\n3835|<code>status:available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code>,\n3836|<code>reason_code:string[1..128]|null</code>,\n3837|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..64]</code>,\n3838|<code>observed_at:timestamp</code>, and <code>extensions</code>. Available has a\n3839|null reason; every other status requires one. <code>DirectoryNodeLimits</code>\n3840|contains exactly <code>max_frame_bytes:uint53[1..8388608]</code>,\n3841|<code>max_scan_instances:uint53[1..65536]</code>,\n3842|<code>max_inventory_take:uint53[1..1000]</code>,\n3843|<code>max_excerpt_count:uint53[0..20]</code>,\n3844|<code>max_excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096]</code>,\n3845|<code>max_enrichment_events:uint53[1..5000]</code>,\n3846|<code>max_enrichment_bytes:uint53[1..4194304]</code>, and\n3847|<code>extensions</code>. Both nested objects are closed except for their listed\n3848|reverse-DNS extension maps.\n3849|\n3850|The exact operation registry and bodies are:\n3851|\n3852|| Operation | Exact request body | Exact success body | Mutation |\n3853|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3854|| <code>manifest</code> | empty object | complete Directory Node Manifest | none |\n3855|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,architecture:amd64\\|arm64,requested_environment_ids:sorted unique environment-id[0..64],requested_capabilities:sorted unique directory-capability[0..8],extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,node_build:DirectoryNodeBuild,policy_digest:digest,environments:EnvironmentObservation[0..256],findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],extensions}</code> | none |\n3856|| <code>scan</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],prior_batch_id:digest|null,cursor:string[1..4096]|null,max_instances:uint53[1..65536],extensions}</code> | <code>{batch:InventoryBatch,environment_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],native_observation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..65536],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,extensions}</code> | directory records only |\n3857|| <code>inventory</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256],fields:sorted unique observation-field[1..32],after:string[1..4096]|null,take:uint53[1..1000],extensions}</code> | <code>{observations:NativeSessionObservation[0..1000],next_cursor:string[1..4096]|null,partial:boolean,extensions}</code> | none |\n3858|| <code>preview</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,roles:sorted unique user\\|assistant[1..2],excerpt_count:uint53[0..20],excerpt_bytes:uint53[0..4096],redaction_policy_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{host_id:UUIDv7,instance_id:digest,observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,excerpts:PreviewExcerpt[0..20],truncated:boolean,redaction_summary:RedactionSummary,freshness:DirectoryFreshness,extensions}</code> | none |\n3859|| <code>enrichment-plan</code> | <code>{request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{accepted:boolean,expected_input_events:uint53,expected_input_bytes:uint53,expected_model_calls:uint53,disclosure_classes:sorted unique string[0..64],blockers:sorted unique string[0..128],extensions}</code> | none |\n3860|| <code>enrichment-run</code> | <code>{operation_id:UUIDv7,request:EnrichmentJobRequest,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | annotation/job records only |\n3861|| <code>enrichment-status</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,extensions}</code> | <code>{job_id:UUIDv7,current_receipt_id:digest,receipt_chain_ids:digest[1..4096],produced_annotation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..16],extensions}</code> | none |\n3862|| <code>continuation-inspect</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,expected_head_digest:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{observation_id:digest,head_digest:digest,management_binding:ManagementBinding,safe_boundary_status:proven\\|unproven\\|not_required,runtime_status:RuntimeExpectation,warnings:sorted unique string[0..256],extensions}</code> | none |\n3863|| <code>runtime-observe</code> | <code>{instance_id:digest,expected_observation_id:digest,extensions}</code> | <code>{runtime:RuntimeExpectation,extensions}</code> | none |\n3864|| <code>doctor</code> | <code>{installation_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256],include_conformance_age:boolean,extensions}</code> | <code>{healthy:boolean,findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096],environment_capabilities:map(digest,map(directory-capability,CapabilityResult))[0..256],cloning_contracts:sorted unique ContractAssertion[0..64],extensions}</code> | none |\n3865|\n3866|Each displayed body is closed; its member types, ordering, and limits are the\n3867|registered Section 10.8 schemas and manifest bounds. The <code>probe</code> row\n3868|shown above is the Request 2.0.0 form; Request 1.0.0 differs only in its closed\n3869|legacy platform vocabulary recorded in the major-binding table. The capability\n3870|registry is exactly <code>directory_discovery</code>,\n3871|<code>directory_incremental_scan</code>, <code>directory_head_digest</code>,\n3872|<code>directory_tail_preview</code>, <code>native_title_read</code>,\n3873|<code>native_runtime_observation</code>,\n3874|<code>existing_session_adoption</code>, and <code>native_resume</code>.\n3875|The closed <code>observation-field</code> registry is exactly\n3876|<code>identity</code>, <code>management</code>, <code>head</code>,\n3877|<code>state</code>, <code>workspace</code>, <code>title</code>,\n3878|<code>counts</code>, <code>preview_status</code>, <code>warnings</code>, and\n3879|<code>timestamps</code>. <code>PreviewExcerpt</code> contains exactly\n3880|<code>role:user|assistant</code>, <code>ordinal:uint53</code>,\n3881|<code>text:string[0..4096]</code>, <code>source_event_id:digest</code>,\n3882|<code>truncated:boolean</code>, and <code>extensions</code>.\n3883|<code>ManagementBinding</code> contains exactly\n3884|<code>state:managed|unmanaged|conflicted</code>,\n3885|<code>session_id:UUIDv7|null</code>,\n3886|<code>provider_identity_record_id:digest|null</code>,\n3887|<code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n3888|<code>extensions</code>; both IDs and non-empty evidence are required exactly\n3889|for managed, both IDs are null for unmanaged, and conflicted retains all\n3890|evidence without choosing a winner. These nested objects are closed except for\n3891|their listed extension maps. <code>DirectoryNodeBuild</code> contains exactly\n3892|<code>node_id:string[1..128]</code>, <code>node_version:semver</code>,\n3893|<code>executable_sha256:digest</code>,\n3894|<code>provider_manifest_digest:digest</code>,\n3895|<code>session_adapter_manifest_digest:digest</code>, and\n3896|<code>extensions</code>; every value equals the current manifest.\n3897|Discovery may degrade for an unknown source tuple only when stable identity and\n3898|bounds remain safe; head/preview/resume/adoption/write/launch fail closed.\n3899|\n3900|<code>scan</code> and <code>enrichment-run</code> use\n3901|<code>(operation,operation_id)</code> idempotency. Repeating the same canonical\n3902|body returns the prior durable result; a changed body is\n3903|<code>idempotency_mismatch</code> without new records. Scan reads only declared\n3904|non-auth roots, publishes observations and its Inventory Batch atomically, and\n3905|never claims that an active prefix is a cloning-safe boundary. Preview requires\n3906|the exact observation/head, defaults to public user/assistant roles, and\n3907|returns bounded redacted terminal-safe text. Raw native IDs and absolute paths\n3908|never leave the source except through an existing AX mutation authority.\n3909|\n3910|## 8. Provider and platform contracts\n3911|\n3912|### 8.1 Matrix notation\n3913|\n3914|Provider and platform matrices use:\n3915|\n3916|- <strong>A</strong>: available from documented or accepted evidence; runtime\n3917|  probe still MUST succeed;\n3918|- <strong>C</strong>: conditional and disabled until the named acceptance gate\n3919|  succeeds for the exact version/platform tuple;\n3920|- <strong>U</strong>: unsupported in v0.3.0 and disabled; and\n3921|- <strong>?</strong>: unknown and disabled because there is no sufficient\n3922|  contract or evidence.\n3923|\n3924|These labels are not aliases. In particular, unknown MUST NOT be rewritten as\n3925|unsupported, and conditional MUST NOT be advertised as available.\n3926|\n3927|### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\n3928|\n3929|| Provider | Durable identity and native location | Resume/import surface | v0.3.0 materialization rule | Required exclusions and limits |\n3930|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3931|| Codex | Session UUID/name; known root <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>. Source absolute cwd is metadata. | <code>codex resume SESSION_ID</code>; current CLI also has <code>codex fork SESSION_ID</code>. | Adapter MUST stage only the closed session objects it has identified, compute the destination cwd mapping, validate discovery by explicit ID, and merge without replacing unrelated sessions. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\n3932|| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\n3933|| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\n3934|| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\n3935|| Antigravity CLI | Conversation UUID plus a destination-authenticated backend/account realm. <code>last_conversations.json</code> maps absolute workspace paths only as local selectors. | <code>agy --conversation UUID</code>, <code>agy -c</code>, and TUI <code>/resume</code>. Desktop-to-CLI picker import is not arbitrary file import. | Materialize the workspace, invoke explicit UUID resume, and allow the provider to rebuild derived cache. A version-aware cache merge MAY map the destination path to UUID. It MUST NOT claim that cache, brain transcript, or SQLite copying recreates a backend-missing conversation. <code>portable_store = false</code>. | OS keyring/account profiles, OAuth/API/MCP secrets, updater locks, live DB/WAL/SHM, sockets, PIDs. Backend resolution is required and a missing UUID MUST fail rather than create a blank replacement. |\n3936|| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\n3937|| Qwen through task-board | The task-board bundle and manager-owned provider identity; there is no v0.2.1 direct claim and no v0.3.0 direct <code>ax-provider-qwen</code> claim. | Official task-board open/adopt only. | U for direct native materialization. A task-board prompt-mode bundle follows Section 9 and remains opaque. | All private manager/provider state except bytes included by the official bundle exporter. |\n3938|| Future plugin | Declared by plugin and exact probe. | Declared by plugin. | Every cell starts ?/disabled. Promotion requires Section 19 acceptance evidence. | Common exclusions plus plugin-specific exclusions. |\n3939|\n3940|Muse and Antigravity rows above are normative uses of the accepted\n3941|<code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code> evidence. The controlled Muse placement probe\n3942|does not create a supported import contract. Antigravity backend resolution is\n3943|native resume but not portable storage.\n3944|\n3945|### 8.3 Capability matrix\n3946|\n3947|| Provider | <code>native_resume</code> | <code>portable_store</code> | <code>managed_pty</code> | <code>appserver</code> | <code>task_board_primary</code> | <code>prompt_spawn</code> | <code>native_goal_binding</code> |\n3948|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n3949|| Codex | A | C | C | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3950|| Claude | A | C | C | U for direct adapter | A through task-board | A through task-board | A through task-board |\n3951|| Gemini CLI | A | C | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3952|| Muse | C by platform/version | U | C | ? | U | A through task-board | U |\n3953|| Antigravity CLI | C: backend realm required | U | C | ? | U | ? | U |\n3954|| Pi | A | C | C | U; Pi RPC is not claimed as this capability | ? | ? | U |\n3955|| Qwen through task-board | U direct | U direct | U direct | U direct | U | A through task-board | U |\n3956|| Future plugin | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? | ? |\n3957|\n3958|For Codex and Claude, task-board owns app-server/thread or PTY mechanics,\n3959|reattach, resume, and goal binding. The direct Claude adapter therefore does\n3960|not advertise <code>appserver</code>. The task-board capability plane and\n3961|direct-provider capability plane MUST NOT be conflated.\n3962|\n3963|### 8.4 Provider/platform matrix\n3964|\n3965|Each cell is <code>native resume / cross-host materialization / managed\n3966|terminal</code>. Task-board-only behavior is stated separately.\n3967|\n3968|| Provider/platform | Status | Normative limit |\n3969|| --- | --- | --- |\n3970|| Codex / macOS | A / C / C | Resume and unrestricted flag are documented; portable store and PTY flush require adapter fixtures. |\n3971|| Codex / Linux | A / C / C | Same; exact distribution and filesystem fixture required. |\n3972|| Codex / WSL2 | A / C / C | Treat as Linux with a Linux store. Repositories SHOULD live below the WSL home, not a Windows-mounted path. |\n3973|| Codex / native Windows | A / C / C | Native CLI is documented. ConPTY, Windows store discovery, file locking, and sandbox mode MUST pass. Windows 11 is the release baseline; Windows 10 is best effort and requires ConPTY. |\n3974|| Claude / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 2.1.229 help confirms UUID resume and unrestricted flag; store transfer remains gated. |\n3975|| Claude / Linux | A / C / C | Provider family documented; distro/PTTY fixture required. |\n3976|| Claude / WSL2 | A / C / C | WSL is provider-documented; use Linux store and path rules. |\n3977|| Claude / native Windows | C / C / C | Windows 10+ with WSL or Git for Windows is documented, but native PowerShell/ConPTY and native store materialization require acceptance. |\n3978|| Gemini / macOS | A / C / C | Official session root, UUID resume, and session-file surface documented. |\n3979|| Gemini / Linux | A / C / C | Ubuntu 20.04+ documented; other distributions conditional. |\n3980|| Gemini / WSL2 | C / C / C | Linux inference; mounted-filesystem, auth, signal, and path-hash tests required. |\n3981|| Gemini / native Windows | A / C / C | Windows 11 24H2+ documented; PowerShell/ConPTY and path-hash tests required. |\n3982|| Muse / macOS arm64 | A for probed 0.1.0 / U / C | Narrow resume probe accepted; current 0.2.1 and full idle/cron fidelity remain unverified. |\n3983|| Muse / macOS amd64 | C / U / C | Artifact/contract exists; not executed. |\n3984|| Muse / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Official launcher artifacts; not executed. |\n3985|| Muse / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux-path inference only. |\n3986|| Muse / native Windows | ? / U / ? | 0.2.1 artifacts exist, but official launcher and persistence contract do not establish support. |\n3987|| Antigravity / macOS amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Resume works only when the authenticated backend realm resolves the UUID; <code>Stop.fullyIdle</code> is documented. |\n3988|| Antigravity / Linux amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; keyring/DBus and PTY tests required. |\n3989|| Antigravity / WSL2 | C / U / ? | Linux inference only; auth, path, signal, and locking tests required. |\n3990|| Antigravity / native Windows amd64 or arm64 | C / U / C | Native family documented; ConPTY, data-root expansion, and file-lock tests required. |\n3991|| Pi / macOS | A / C / C | Installed 0.73.1 help verifies session surfaces and default full tool set. |\n3992|| Pi / Linux | C / C / C | Cross-platform Node/package behavior is plausible but exact 0.73.1 acceptance is required. |\n3993|| Pi / WSL2 | C / C / C | Treat as Linux only after path/signal/auth tests. |\n3994|| Pi / native Windows | C / C / C | Provider platform notes exist; exact 0.73.1 store, shell, and ConPTY behavior is unverified. |\n3995|| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\n3996|| Future plugin / any | ? / ? / ? | Disabled until a tuple-specific probe and acceptance record exist. |\n3997|\n3998|The release MUST NOT collapse WSL2 and native Windows into one row. An adapter\n3999|accepted in WSL2 does not establish native Windows support.\n4000|\n4001|## 9. Task-board integration\n4002|\n4003|### 9.1 Ownership boundary\n4004|\n4005|Task-board is both a provider-launch abstraction and a distinct persistence\n4006|boundary. <code>tb-sessiond</code> owns private Codex app-server/thread state,\n4007|Claude PTY state, reattach mechanics, provider resume, and goal bindings.\n4008|<code>ax</code> MUST NOT inspect manager databases, private session records,\n4009|provider process files, or authentication state.\n4010|\n4011|The only portable interface is the official\n4012|<code>urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>\n4013|contract. Its initial public creation surface is <code>launch</code>; its bundle\n4014|boundary uses <code>export</code>, <code>import</code>, <code>open</code>, and\n4015|<code>adopt</code>; its public lifecycle controls are <code>status</code>,\n4016|<code>stop</code>, and <code>resume</code>. Until\n4017|task-board advertises this exact bridge version and the required operations,\n4018|task-board takeover MUST report\n4019|<code>task_board_bridge_unavailable</code>. Existing whole-board archive\n4020|commands are not a substitute.\n4021|\n4022|### 9.2 Official bridge command surface\n4023|\n4024|The required CLI facade is:\n4025|\n4026|~~~shell\n4027|task-board session launch --operation-id OPERATION_ID --request REQUEST_FILE --json\n4028|task-board session status --session SESSION_REF --json\n4029|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode snapshot --json\n4030|task-board session export --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --bundle FILE --format tb-session-bundle-v1 --mode handoff --json\n4031|task-board session import --operation-id OPERATION_ID --bundle FILE --staging-root DIR --json\n4032|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode dormant-replica --json\n4033|task-board session open --operation-id OPERATION_ID --import-token TOKEN --mode fork --new-session SESSION_ID --json\n4034|task-board session adopt --operation-id OPERATION_ID --open-token TOKEN --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --json\n4035|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode graceful --control-token TOKEN --json\n4036|task-board session stop --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --mode force --json\n4037|task-board session resume --operation-id OPERATION_ID --session SESSION_REF --ax-session SESSION_ID --lease-epoch EPOCH --lease-id LEASE_ID --profile standard|yolo --json\n4038|~~~\n4039|\n4040|Every command MUST print exactly one schema-versioned JSON result to stdout and\n4041|diagnostics to stderr. The bridge MAY use an internal local API, but the\n4042|semantics and bundle bytes MUST be identical.\n4043|\n4044|<code>REQUEST_FILE</code> is an owner-only, machine-local JSON file containing\n4045|exactly the logical <code>launch</code> request body below; the duplicated\n4046|<code>operation_id</code> MUST equal the flag. It contains no credential values\n4047|and MUST be removed after a terminal bridge result. Every mutating facade\n4048|requires the caller-supplied <code>--operation-id</code>; task-board MUST NOT\n4049|replace it with an internally generated value. This makes the exact invocation\n4050|repeatable after a lost response.\n4051|\n4052|The result envelope uses the bridge protocol version independently of the\n4053|bundle schema:\n4054|\n4055|~~~json\n4056|{\n4057|  \"protocol\": \"urn:ax:protocol:task-board-bridge\",\n4058|  \"protocol_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n4059|  \"operation\": \"export\",\n4060|  \"ok\": true,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
