rule is Section 19.3.\n16120|\n16121|## Appendix C. Evidence and primary references\n16122|\n16123|Provider behavior is version-sensitive. These references support the stated\n16124|surface while the matrices retain the stricter tuple-specific gates:\n16125|\n16126|1. Settled decisions attached to <code>TASK-260819-1h306n</code>.\n16127|2. Accepted <code>TASK-260819-1ecd6x</code>\n16128|   [Muse and Antigravity evidence report](.research/260819_muse-antigravity-native-store-contracts.md),\n16129|   including its primary-source ledger and accepted limitations.\n16130|3. [Official Codex CLI command reference](https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference/)\n16131|   for resume/fork and unrestricted flags.\n16132|4. [Official Codex WSL guidance](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/windows/wsl)\n16133|   and [native Windows sandbox guidance](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/windows/windows-sandbox).\n16134|5. [Anthropic Claude Code setup](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/getting-started)\n16135|   plus the locally probed Claude Code 2.1.229 help surface.\n16136|6. [Gemini CLI session management](https://geminicli.com/docs/cli/session-management/)\n16137|   and [installation requirements](https://geminicli.com/docs/get-started/installation/),\n16138|   plus locally probed Gemini CLI 0.54.4 help.\n16139|7. [Pi usage/session documentation](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md)\n16140|   and [Pi settings/session-directory documentation](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md),\n16141|   plus locally probed Pi 0.73.1 help.\n16142|8. Accepted <code>TASK-260829-1bhmis</code>\n16143|   [Superlogical integration-surface report](.research/260829_superlogical-integration-surface.md),\n16144|   based on the [official product site](https://www.superlogical.com/),\n16145|   [Mitchell Hashimoto's product-direction note](https://mitchellh.com/writing/superlogical),\n16146|   and the [official GitHub organization](https://github.com/superlogical), all\n16147|   retrieved 2026-08-29. These sources establish only the bounded future-product\n16148|   observations in Section 4.E; they establish no release, AX adapter, API, SDK,\n16149|   backend ID, compatibility, capability, ownership, transport, or conformance\n16150|   claim.\n16151|\n16152|Host-channel building blocks were checked 2026-09-08 against\n16153|[TLS 1.3 (RFC 8446)](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8446),\n16154|[X.509 (RFC 5280)](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5280),\n16155|[Go TLS](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/tls),\n16156|[Go X.509](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/x509),\n16157|[OpenSSH server restrictions](https://man.openbsd.org/sshd.8), and\n16158|[native Tailscale SSH](https://tailscale.com/docs/features/tailscale-ssh).\n16159|The issuance, enrollment, pinning and generation policy is AX\n16160|Section 11.10 design, not a claim that those sources implement AX. The\n16161|[host-channel source report](.research/260908_host-channel-profile.md) records\n16162|the design rationale and evidence limits.\n16163|\n16164|Local help probes are evidence only for the exact installed versions and macOS\n16165|host. They do not establish another platform cell.\n16166|\n16167|## Appendix D. Normative contract fixture catalog\n16168|\n16169|### D.1 Fixture execution rules\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c52b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":240,"recorded_at":1780531400000475,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2c7753720591d0c902ed8a4943","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(2084 line(s) above)\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2088|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2089|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2090|\n2091|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2092|| --- | --- | --- |\n2093|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2094|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2095|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2096|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2097|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2098|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2099|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2100|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2101|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2102|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n2103|| <code>logical_workspace_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Member of the Session Record workspace group |\n2104|| <code>backend_realm_fingerprint</code> | digest or null | Non-secret fingerprint; non-null when backend/account realm is a resume precondition |\n2105|| <code>opaque_identity</code> | map(provider-identity-key,string[1..1024])[0..32] | Explicit adapter data map defined below |\n2106|| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Identifying owner host |\n2107|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2108|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2109|\n2110|A provider-identity key matches <code>[a-z][a-z0-9_.-]{0,63}</code>. Map keys\n2111|are data rather than schema members; values are non-secret strings only. This\n2112|is the sole provider-defined identity-data surface in version 1.0.0. It MUST\n2113|NOT contain an absolute path, credential, environment value, PID, socket,\n2114|terminal ID, or mutable cache selector. Structured or binary provider data\n2115|belongs in a content-addressed provider manifest, not this map.\n2116|\n2117|An absolute workspace path MAY appear only as source observation metadata. It\n2118|MUST NOT be part of the cross-host identity. The destination adapter MUST\n2119|derive native path keys from the destination workspace mapping.\n2120|\n2121|Normative negative fixtures are: unknown <code>identity_kind</code>; absent\n2122|<code>opaque_identity</code>; a map value that is an object instead of a\n2123|string; an absolute source path in that map; or an Antigravity\n2124|<code>backend_conversation_uuid</code> with null realm fingerprint. Each MUST\n2125|fail schema or provider-identity validation. A backend fingerprint is optional\n2126|for the other kinds unless that provider's Section 8 contract requires it.\n2127|\n2128|Normative example:\n2129|\n2130|~~~json\n2131|{\n2132|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:provider-identity\",\n2133|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2134|  \"record_id\": \"sha256:c879d766da67a8cfb3a3f6eae2234faa5d52d8df987496eae2218f40e5e220c2\",\n2135|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2136|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2137|  \"provider_id\": \"antigravity\",\n2138|  \"provider_version\": \"1.1.14\",\n2139|  \"provider_version_range\": \">=1.1.14 <1.2.0\",\n2140|  \"native_session_id\": \"11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555\",\n2141|  \"identity_kind\": \"backend_conversation_uuid\",\n2142|  \"logical_workspace_id\": \"0198f4c8-6c30-7d44-8d5e-1234567890ab\",\n2143|  \"backend_realm_fingerprint\": \"sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaad\",\n2144|  \"opaque_identity\": {},\n2145|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2146|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:45.000Z\",\n2147|  \"extensions\": {}\n2148|}\n2149|~~~\n2150|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
