{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c639","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":375,"recorded_at":1780531400000745,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2c-c544-7ee3-a515-3e11903d2229"},"task_id":"01a0ae2c-c544-7ee3-a515-3e11903d2229","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2c-c544-7ee3-a515-3e11903d2229","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/protocol.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"io\"\n7|\t\"math\"\n8|\t\"strconv\"\n9|\t\"strings\"\n10|\t\"time\"\n11|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n12|\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axerror\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|// Wire constants of pinned specification Section 7.2. The protocol\n18|// identifier and version are exact: a different major is never negotiated,\n19|// and anything other than 2.0.0 on the wire is refused or reported as a\n20|// major mismatch, never accepted.\n21|const (\n22|\t// ProtocolID is the exact protocol member every request and response\n23|\t// envelope carries.\n24|\tProtocolID = \"urn:ax:protocol:provider\"\n25|\t// ProtocolVersion is the exact protocol_version member this host\n26|\t// writes and the only one it accepts a response under.\n27|\tProtocolVersion = \"2.0.0\"\n28|\t// ProtocolMajor is the major this host implements. Responses under\n29|\t// any other recognizable major are reported as incompatible_protocol\n30|\t// without trusting their payload.\n31|\tProtocolMajor = 2\n32|\t// MaxFrameBytes bounds one JSONL line in either direction: Section\n33|\t// 7.2 requires every line to be one complete UTF-8 JSON object no\n34|\t// larger than 8 MiB.\n35|\tMaxFrameBytes = 8 << 20\n36|\t// StderrCapBytes caps captured plugin stderr. It is an implementation\n37|\t// resource bound, not a protocol limit: diagnostics beyond it are\n38|\t// dropped. Failure details carry the failure class and member names\n39|\t// only, never stderr content.\n40|\tStderrCapBytes = 1 << 20\n41|)\n42|\n43|// Operation names one Section 7.5 registry entry. The registry is closed:\n44|// dispatch refuses any other name locally, before any process starts.\n45|type Operation string\n46|\n47|// Section 7.5 operation registry in the Section 7.3 manifest order. The\n48|// inventory test derives this list from the pinned specification text and\n49|// requires exact ordered equality, so a dropped, added, or reordered entry\n50|// reddens there rather than passing silently.\n51|const (\n52|\tOpManifest            Operation = \"manifest\"\n53|\tOpProbe               Operation = \"probe\"\n54|\tOpLaunch              Operation = \"launch\"\n55|\tOpIdentifySession     Operation = \"identify-session\"\n56|\tOpQuiesce             Operation = \"quiesce\"\n57|\tOpNativeStorePlan     Operation = \"native-store-plan\"\n58|\tOpCapture             Operation = \"capture\"\n59|\tOpMaterialize         Operation = \"materialize\"\n60|\tOpMaterializeStatus   Operation = \"materialize-status\"\n61|\tOpMaterializeCommit   Operation = \"materialize-commit\"\n62|\tOpMaterializeRollback Operation = \"materialize-rollback\"\n63|\tOpResume              Operation = \"resume\"\n64|\tOpFork                Operation = \"fork\"\n65|\tOpStop                Operation = \"stop\"\n66|\tOpDoctor              Operation = \"doctor\"\n67|)\n68|\n69|// operationOrder is the single construction site of the dispatch registry.\n70|var operationOrder = []Operation{\n71|\tOpManifest,\n72|\tOpProbe,\n73|\tOpLaunch,\n74|\tOpIdentifySession,\n75|\tOpQuiesce,\n76|\tOpNativeStorePlan,\n77|\tOpCapture,\n78|\tOpMaterialize,\n79|\tOpMaterializeStatus,\n80|\tOpMaterializeCommit,\n81|\tOpMaterializeRollback,\n82|\tOpResume,\n83|\tOpFork,\n84|\tOpStop,\n85|\tOpDoctor,\n86|}\n87|\n88|// Operations returns the dispatch registry in manifest order. The result\n89|// is a copy; the registry cannot be mutated through it.\n90|func Operations() []string {\n91|\tout := make([]string, 0, len(operationOrder))\n92|\tfor _, operation := range operationOrder {\n93|\t\tout = append(out, string(operation))\n94|\t}\n95|\treturn out\n96|}\n97|\n98|// validOperation reports whether the name is a registry member.\n99|func validOperation(name string) bool {\n100|\tfor _, operation := range operationOrder {\n101|\t\tif string(operation) == name {\n102|\t\t\treturn true\n103|\t\t}\n104|\t}\n105|\treturn false\n106|}\n107|\n108|// The refusal constructors below are declared as variables so the\n109|// inventory gate can observe every exercised refusal site. Each is the\n110|// single construction site for its failure class; production code must\n111|// not build *axerror.Error any other way.\n112|//\n113|// failInvalid reports a caller error caught before any process starts:\n114|// an unknown operation, a stale deadline, or an unframeable request body.\n115|// failProtocol reports an unusable plugin frame through the Section 15.1\n116|// provider-stdio otherwise branch. failMismatch reports a recognizable\n117|// major mismatch through the same table's mismatch branch, without\n118|// trusting the foreign payload. failProcess reports a crash or transport\n119|// failure. failTimeout reports a plugin that exceeded its request\n120|// deadline. failIntegrity reports a status observation that cannot be\n121|// reconciled to durable state.\n122|var failInvalid = func(detail string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n123|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{Version: axerror.Version100, Code: \"invalid_config\", Message: \"provider host refused the request: \" + detail, Details: axerror.Details{}})\n124|}\n125|\n126|var failProtocol = func(detail string, member string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n127|\treturn axerror.LocalFromUntrusted(axerror.SurfaceProviderStdio, axerror.OutcomeUnusableFrame, \"provider host rejected the plugin frame: \"+detail, axerror.NoIDs(), axerror.Details{\"member\": member}, nil)\n128|}\n129|\n130|var failMismatch = func(detail string, observed string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n131|\treturn axerror.LocalFromUntrusted(axerror.SurfaceProviderStdio, axerror.OutcomeRecognizableMajorMismatch, \"provider host rejected a foreign protocol major: \"+detail, axerror.NoIDs(), axerror.Details{\"observed\": observed}, nil)\n132|}\n133|\n134|var failProcess = func(detail string, cause error) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n135|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{Version: axerror.Version100, Code: \"provider_process_failed\", Message: \"provider plugin process failed: \" + detail, Details: axerror.Details{}, Cause: cause})\n136|}\n137|\n138|var failTimeout = func(detail string, millis int64) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n139|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{Version: axerror.Version100, Code: \"provider_timeout\", Message: \"provider plugin exceeded its deadline: \" + detail, Details: axerror.Details{\"deadline_ms\": json.Number(strconv.FormatInt(millis, 10))}})\n140|}\n141|\n142|var failIntegrity = func(detail string, statusState string, materializationID string, transactionID string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n143|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{Version: axerror.Version100, Code: \"integrity_failure\", Message: \"provider status observation is not durable state: \" + detail, Details: axerror.Details{\"status_state\": statusState, \"materialization_id\": materializationID, \"transaction_id\": transactionID}})\n144|}\n145|\n146|// failMappingUnavailable reports the Section 2.4 resume failure:\n147|// the adapter cannot map the stored profile for the probed\n148|// provider version. The details name the provider, the exact\n149|// probed version, and the profile that had no mapping.\n150|var failMappingUnavailable = func(detail string, providerID string, providerVersion string, profile string) (*axerror.Error, error) {\n151|\treturn axerror.New(axerror.Spec{Version: axerror.Version100, Code: \"profile_mapping_unavailable\", Message: \"provider host cannot map the stored profile: \" + detail, Details: axerror.Details{\"provider_id\": providerID, \"provider_version\": providerVersion, \"profile\": profile}})\n152|}\n153|\n154|// Request is one Section 7.2 request envelope. Body crosses the transport\n155|// opaquely: it must be a JSON object, and its members are interpreted by\n156|// the operation layer, except for the status recovery read.\n157|type Request struct {\n158|\tOperation Operation\n159|\tRequestID scalar.UUIDv7\n160|\tDeadline  scalar.Timestamp\n161|\tBody      json.RawMessage\n162|}\n163|\n164|// Response is one accepted success envelope. Body is the raw\n165|// operation-specific object for the operation layer to interpret. A\n166|// failure envelope never produces a Response: DecodeResponse returns the\n167|// bound child error instead, and a failure envelope carrying a body is\n168|// refused outright.\n169|type Response struct {\n170|\tBody json.RawMessage\n171|}\n172|\n173|// wireRequest is the exact emitted member set: protocol, protocol_version,\n174|// request_id, operation, deadline, and body, in this fixed order.\n175|type wireRequest struct {\n176|\tProtocol        string           `json:\"protocol\"`\n177|\tProtocolVersion string           `json:\"protocol_version\"`\n178|\tRequestID       scalar.UUIDv7    `json:\"request_id\"`\n179|\tOperation       string           `json:\"operation\"`\n180|\tDeadline        scalar.Timestamp `json:\"deadline\"`\n181|\tBody            json.RawMessage  `json:\"body\"`\n182|}\n183|\n184|// EncodeRequest frames one request as a single JSONL line without the\n185|// terminator. The deadline must be in the future at now, which the caller\n186|// supplies so tests stay deterministic; Host passes its clock.\n187|func EncodeRequest(req Request, now time.Time) ([]byte, error) {\n188|\tframe, _, err := encodeFrame(req, now)\n189|\treturn frame, err\n190|}\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
