{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":944,"recorded_at":1780531400001883,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae32-90a4-7cb2-9377-19384e91bdb6"},"task_id":"01a0ae32-90a4-7cb2-9377-19384e91bdb6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae32-90a4-7cb2-9377-19384e91bdb6","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-32-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json'))\\nkinds={}\\nfor e in d['ownership']:\\n    kinds.setdefault(e.get('kind'),[]).append(e)\\nprint({k:len(v) for k,v in kinds.items()})\\nfor e in kinds.get('section',[])[:3]:\\n    print(json.dumps(e,indent=1)[:900]); print('...')\\nprint('acceptance_cases:', len(d.get('acceptance_cases',[])))\\nprint(json.dumps(d['acceptance_cases'][0],indent=1)[:600] if d.get('acceptance_cases') else None)\\nprint('unowned_sections:', d.get('unowned_sections'))\\n\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Survey ownership kinds and section entries\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{'contract': 1, 'normative_section': 2, 'section_binding': 56, 'fixture': 2}\\nacceptance_cases: 101\\n{\\n \\\"id\\\": \\\"source-pin-exact\\\",\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Current\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"tests\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/specpin/pin_test.go\\\",\\n   \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"TestCurrentPinsPublishedV050Source\\\"\\n  }\\n ]\\n}\\nunowned_sections: [{'key': 'section:2.2', 'gap': 'Section 2.2 states the unconditional lease, replica, replication, tombstone and capability invariants of the product, and none of them is implemented here. The binding this entry replaces named validateSessionRecordCommon, which validates Session Record shape and the execution-profile enum value only.', 'evidence': 'The repository contains no lease, epoch, replica, takeover, tombstone or replication implementation: internal/canonicaljson validates record shape, internal/localstore stores immutable objects and rebuilds a local index, and the two acceptance cases the replaced binding named are canonical-identity cases.'}, {'key': 'section:18.4', 'gap': 'Section 18.4 requires audit retention - the exact Section 5.2 event types for lease change, force confirmation, managed replacement, task-board launch and adoption and tombstone issuance and resolution, and retention of the event and every referenced immutable object for as long as the Session Record. No retention, expiry or garbage-collection rule is implemented.', 'evidence': 'internal/localstore/projection.go opens, rebuilds and recovers the SQLite projection and installs immutable blobs; it declares no retention, expiry or garbage-collection behaviour, and the binding this entry replaces named OpenProjection with the same two storage acceptance cases already used by the Section 3.3 binding.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.1', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.1 requires SSH host-channel launch with exclusive TLS 1.3, ALPN ax-host/1 and full mutual certificate authentication; no launcher, TLS endpoint or handshake exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9.', 'evidence': 'The repository carries no TLS, X.509 or SSH-launch code: provhost speaks the provider-plugin protocol over stdio, secprim checks argv, environment and paths, and the mesh RPC layer is catalog vocabulary without a transport.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.2', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.2 requires certificate issuance into a machine-local trust store with enrolled roots and exact leaf checks; no issuance, store or enrollment implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.', 'evidence': 'No certificate, key custody or trust-store code exists: internal/config reads TOML only, internal/localstore keeps blobs and a SQLite projection, and the two new pin fixtures are byte identities without a Go consumer.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.3', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.3 requires credential rotation, revocation and authorization generations that refuse stale trust; no rotation or revocation implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.', 'evidence': 'Nothing in the tree rotates or revokes credentials: there is no credential store to rotate, no revocation list reader, and no authorization-generation check outside the specification text.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.4', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.4 bounds host-channel assurance and executable fixture conformance; no assurance measurement or host-channel fixture runner exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.', 'evidence': 'The pinned host_channel_conformance fixture is a lock identity only: internal/secconftest runs crash, hostile and fuzz harnesses over local surfaces and reads no upstream conformance fixture.'}, {'key': 'section:11.10.5', 'gap': 'Section 11.10.5 defines the upstream public synthetic admission validator, not a runtime requirement to parse SPEC.md during AX host admission. Its source vectors do not establish AX runtime conformance; production host-channel conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.', 'evidence': 'The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from policy witnesses. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-2x16gz owns consuming this evidence and proving real AX host admission.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.1', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.1 requires literal first-at source-qualified selector grammar with configured source-index resolution; no selector parser or source index exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.', 'evidence': 'No CLI session commands exist at all: the tree builds no ax binary, sessadapter SourceSelector validates directory-protocol members rather than CLI selectors, and Section 2.3 name precedence is shape validation only.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.2', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.2 requires resolve-once fact binding with revalidation before execution; no selection planner or bound-fact store exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.', 'evidence': 'Nothing binds selection facts to execution: there is no selector resolver whose output could go stale, and no plan revalidation reads a source index.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.3', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.3 binds the five Structured Error 1.4.0 codes to exits exclusively inside CLI Result 5; no Go mapping carries those codes. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.', 'evidence': 'The axerror registry is closed over Structured Error 1.0.0 through 1.3.0 with 109 codes; the 1.4.0 code-to-exit mapping has no implementation and no emitter.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.4', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.4 requires interrupted record-only creation with authoritative bootstrap recovery; no chooser, bootstrap creation or recovery flow exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1wb06o.', 'evidence': 'No session creation path exists in the tree: there is no CLI create command, no chooser, and no bootstrap lease issuance that an interruption could leave record-only.'}, {'key': 'section:14.7.5', 'gap': 'Section 14.7.5 defines the upstream selector publication evaluator and its source-only case inventory. Source publication does not attest runtime provenance, temporal boundaries or running AX implementation; product selector conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.', 'evidence': 'The pinned section explicitly distinguishes the publication evaluator from runtime authority/durability obligations. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-1i7bqr owns product-level composed conformance using the shared resolver and lifecycle APIs.'}]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6665,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1667,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
