{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dae9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2b-e184-7c10-8d9d-bac4c231b352"},"sequence":3023,"recorded_at":1780531400006041,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"be9157de-ded3-4e9d-94df-e7cb793fb0f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae43-5fcb-7f51-9892-c0713a202187"},"task_id":"01a0ae43-5fcb-7f51-9892-c0713a202187","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae43-5fcb-7f51-9892-c0713a202187","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-72-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-315721/worktree && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json'))\\nfor e in d['ownership']:\\n    if e.get('kind')=='section_binding' and e.get('coverage') in ('full','partial','sliver'):\\n        print(json.dumps(e,indent=1)[:1400]); print('======')\\n\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Show measured-coverage binding examples\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:6.2\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/config/schema.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Decode\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"full\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"6.2#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 2433,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"MUST be <code>conpty</code>. WSL2 configuration uses Linux paths and <code>platform = \\\\\\\"wsl2\\\\\\\"</code>.\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ]\\n}\\n======\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:10.3\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/canonicaljson/closed_shapes.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"validateBlobDescriptor\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"scalar-bounded-integer-validation\\\",\\n  \\\"scalar-digest-validation\\\",\\n  \\\"canonical-identity-refusal\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"sliver\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"validateBlobDescriptor enforces the Section 10.3 chunk offset invariant, but the two receiver clauses - validate every chunk before marking it present, and validate the complete blob after assembly - have no implementation because no transfer receiver exists.\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"10.3#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 4729,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"<code>chunk_id:digest</code>. It has no extension map. Offset MUST equal index times 4,194,304; every non-final chunk has that exact size.\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"canonical-identity-refusal\\\"\\n   ]\\n  }\\n ]\\n}\\n======\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:15.1\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/axerror/axerror.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"New\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"structured-error-exact-object\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-shape-refusal\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-detail-redaction\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-detail-inertness\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-static-binding\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-unknown-code-reader\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-local-untrusted\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-message-independence\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-historical-envelopes\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-identity-precedence\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-common-data-model\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; this repository contains no RPC hello builder at all, so BindingFor is a static table with no negotiation path rather than a refusal of one. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no\\n======\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:15.3\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/axerror/registry.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ExitCodeFor\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"structured-error-code-exit-registry\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-unknown-code-reader\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-typed-details\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-historical-envelopes\\\",\\n  \\\"structured-error-exit-status-fan-in\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame is built anywhere in this repository, and the closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hello path and carries no Structured Error code, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\\\",\\n \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"15.3#1\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 14860,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"unknown code retains the envelope's exit class and MUST NOT be interpreted as\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"structured-error-unknown-code-reader\\\",\\n    \\\"cli-result-historical-envelopes\\\"\\n   ]\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"id\\\": \\\"15.3#2\\\",\\n   \\\"line\\\": 14872,\\n   \\\"excerpt\\\": \\\"continues to use <code>interactive_choice_required</code>. Implementations MUST\\\",\\n   \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n    \\\"structured-error-code-exit-registry\\\",\\n    \\\"structured-error-typed-details\\\"\\n   ]\\n======\\n{\\n \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n \\\"keys\\\": [\\n  \\\"section:14.2\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"production\\\": {\\n  \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/cliresult/output.go\\\",\\n  \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"Emit\\\"\\n },\\n \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n  \\\"cli-result-envelope-exact\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-envelope-refusal\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-body-closure\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-common-flags\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-yes-admission\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-json-one-document\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-destructive-confirmation\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-expectation-flags\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-rpc-serve-rejects-json\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-takeover-adoption\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-exit-status-mapping\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-unimplemented-surface-refusal\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-machine-reading\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-stderr-independence\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-historical-envelopes\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-message-independence\\\",\\n  \\\"cli-result-identity-precedence\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n \\\"gap\\\": \\\"One of the nine Section 14.2 clauses stays unimplemented here. Clause 14.2#6 requires the process exit status to equal the failure object's exit_code. Emit resolves that exact status from the Structured Error registry and returns it, and ExitStatus reports it without emitting, but this repository builds no ax binary: the only os.Exit calls in the tree are the exit(1) failure paths of cataloggen and tracecheck, so no process in this repository ever terminates with a CLI failure status and the process-level half of 14.2#6 is unowned. Read checks the same equality from the consuming side and re\\n======\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5586,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1397,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
